{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'correspondence|origin-bindings|provenance|site-c1-binding' src/dev/latte_oracle_tables.clj test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc collab/yang-clojure/1794344088000-orchestrator-cc3-d1-mob-reconciliation.md\"","aggregated_output":"collab/yang-clojure/1794344088000-orchestrator-cc3-d1-mob-reconciliation.md:20:The orchestrator spot-checked load-bearing claims before reconciliation: `slice9_site_tables.edn` has no readers outside `latte_oracle_test.clj` + docs (grep); `derive.cljc` stack-image side-table carries only `:closure`/`:var` diagnostics, no `:call` provenance (source read). Both deepseek claims held.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794344088000-orchestrator-cc3-d1-mob-reconciliation.md:24:All three approve route (a): extend `yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc` + `semantic/derive.cljc` (native-image PC→K reconstruction is LOWERING, not evaluator runtime — inside the yang.clojure seat's authorized surface) and bind oracle sites via verified static correspondence. No `ast_walker`/`semantic`/`stack`/`register` runtime changes; general runtime caller-K propagation remains a continuation-seat boundary item (3/3 agree it is NOT required for cc3 or D1).\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794344088000-orchestrator-cc3-d1-mob-reconciliation.md:29:3. **Static ≠ runtime** (astra): the shared \"latest site\" guest cell cannot prove preservation across suspension/interleaving; cc3 verifies its correspondence claims in both lanes and refuses ambiguous cases; it must not claim migration coverage.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794344088000-orchestrator-cc3-d1-mob-reconciliation.md:30:4. **Provenance must become durable** (deepseek, argon): `publish-closure!` (`publish.cljc:312`) and `yin.repl` (`repl.cljc:158`) discard `:provenance` today; cc3 persists it as a side artifact OUTSIDE the schema-1 manifest hash (the cc1 precedent, `publish.cljc:352-367`).\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794344088000-orchestrator-cc3-d1-mob-reconciliation.md:36:Do NOT upgrade `slice9_site_tables.edn` in place. D1 is a separately addressed `:yang.correspondence/schema 1` record (companion `test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_correspondence.edn`) whose `:evidence` names the `:version 1` tables VERBATIM (design §4.1: \"do not project a subset or copy its rows into a second durable site-table shape\"; §4.2: \"D1 does not revise old site tables\"). K-keyed access is a verified query through the `:origin-bindings` relation, not a second attribution table. Integer site ids are scoped per compilation (they restart); historical runs without retained admissions never acquire invented origins — a new recorded run is produced instead (owner ruling U: origins are never minted).\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794344088000-orchestrator-cc3-d1-mob-reconciliation.md:42:- argon + astra: D1's independent verification lands BEFORE cc4's final four-host/budget acceptance (design §8 step 4→5: a frontend acceptance that relies on correspondence cites a completed D1 verification; astra adds that cc4's final measurements must include D1's retained reconstruction inputs).\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794344088000-orchestrator-cc3-d1-mob-reconciliation.md:48:1. cc3's brief will carry Q1's six conditions as acceptance criteria, and Q2's format as the D1-adjacent constraint (cc3 publishes the provenance side artifact; D1 consumes it).\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:317:      (and claim (contains? claim :wrapper-provenance))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:318:      (refusal :yin.link.publish/wrapper-provenance claim)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:326:            ;; validated C1 rows so every image's call provenance is\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:337:                                       :call-provenance (:call-provenance sem-proj)}))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:342:                                          :call-provenance (:call-provenance sem-proj)}))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publi