{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'exception.track|registry|one.writer' collab/yang-clojure | head -35\"","aggregated_output":"collab/yang-clojure/1794300271000-engineer-exception-r3-verify-resume.prompt.md:21:2. The spec: `collab/exception-track/1794960000000-owner-ruling-exception-uniformity-v2.md` §R3, §R5.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794343683000-architect-cc3-d1-mob.gemini-4-argon-high.stdout.log:1:{\"conversation_id\":\"4b7ced60-62f7-4668-82a3-c72aececc945\",\"status\":\"SUCCESS\",\"response\":\"Completed-GMT: 2026-11-10 20:52:00 GMT\\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-11 03:52:00 +0700\\n\\nQ1 VERDICT: SUFFICIENT WITH THREE BOUNDARY-RESPECTING LOWERING REQUIREMENTS (native-image PC→K reconstruction is in `cc3` scope inside `derive.cljc`/`publish.cljc`; runtime evaluator caller-K propagation is a continuation-seat boundary item not required for `cc3` or `D1`).\\nQ2 VERDICT: (ii) SEPARATE COMPANION FILE `test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_correspondence.edn` REFERENCING VERBATIM `:version 1` `slice9_site_tables.edn`.\\nQ3 VERDICT: AMEND ORDER TO `cc2 → cc3 → D1 → cc4` (`D1` before `cc4`).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Question 1 — `cc3` Route Sufficiency\\n\\n`Q1 VERDICT: SUFFICIENT WITH THREE BOUNDARY-RESPECTING LOWERING REQUIREMENTS (native-image PC→K reconstruction is in cc3 scope inside derive.cljc/publish.cljc; runtime evaluator caller-K propagation is a continuation-seat boundary item not required for cc3 or D1).`\\n\\n### Evidence \\u0026 Severity-Ordered Defect Analysis for Route (a)\\n\\nRoute (a) — extending [`src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc), [`src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/derive.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/derive.cljc), [`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc), and [`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj) without editing any evaluator (`ast_walker.cljc`, `semantic.cljc`, `debruijn/stack.cljc`, `debruijn_register_effects.cljc`) — **is sufficient** to meet the Design §2.4, §2.5, and §4.2 acceptance bar, provided `cc3` addresses three concrete defects in the current naive lowering/oracle plumbing:\\n\\n1. **[P1 — Per-Occurrence Origin Loss in `linearize/project-rows`] (`src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc:188-214`, `src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:312`)**:\\n   - **What fails if unaddressed**: [`linearize/project-rows`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc#L200-L214) currently accepts only a single scalar `origin` (`(when-not (or (nil? origin) (vm/occurrence-origin? origin)) ...)`) and stamps that single `origin` onto every PC (`(mapv (fn [pc [_ path]] [pc origin root path]) (range) sources)`), omitting `segment-address`. Under Owner Ruling U1 ([`1795310000000:13`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1795310000000-owner-ruling-occurrence-identity-unitarity.md#L13)) and `cc1`'s [`macro/final-call-site-metadata`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc#L1598-L1627), a post-expansion tree contains **heterogeneous per-occurrence origins**: `[:source medium batch j]` for retained source applications and `[:expansion record-address]` for macro-generated applications. Passing a single `origin` to `project-rows` would overwrite `[:expansion record-address]` origins on macro-generated `:call` instructions and fail Design §2.4/§4.2 step 5 reconstruction.\\n   - **Minimal boundary-respecting remedy**: Extend `linearize/project-rows` (or add a provenance-projection arity/helper in `linearize.cljc`) to accept an optional `path -\\u003e origin` lookup map (derived from the C1 side table `[origin root-address path :yang/call-site 1]`) alongside the fallback admission `origin`, and prepend `segment-address` (`(:address result)`, i.e. `(ucf/code-address code)` at [`linearize.cljc:211`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc#L211)) so each emitted provenance row has the canonical 5-tuple shape `[segment-address pc origin root-address path]` ([`docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:447,920-924`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md#L447)). In [`linearize/project-datoms`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc#L298-L302), `flatten-tree` already computes `sources` as `[[id path] ...]` and discards `path` at line 302 (`(mapv (fn [pc [id _]] [pc id]) (range) sources)`); retain `path` or provide the entity-to-occurrence bridge with [`encoder/datom-entity-occurrences`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc#L67-L93) as required by Design §2.4 ([`1794670000000:77`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L77)).\\n\\n2. **[P1 — Native-Image `PC → K` Reconstruction Scope \\u0026 Validator Contract Guard] (`src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/derive.cljc:60-184`, `src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc:2121-2133`, `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc:699-707`)**:\\n   - **Scope classification**: Native-image `PC → K` reconstruction (Design §2.4, [`1794670000000:75`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L75)) is **in `cc3` scope** because it is a pure static lowering derivation in `derive.cljc` and `publish.cljc` — it requires **zero** evaluator/runtime changes.\\n   - **How it works statically**:\\n     - `derive/resolve` ([`derive.cljc:21-42`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/derive.cljc#L21-L42)) parses the semantic vector `v` via [`code/parse`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/code.cljc#L349-L435) into expression trees `{:op mnemonic :pc semantic-pc :children [...]}` while preserving semantic PCs.\\n     - `derive/register-image` ([`derive.cljc:154-184`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/derive.cljc#L154-L184)) preserves `v`'s exact instruction indices (`(mapv (fn [pc t] ...) (range (count rv)) rv)` at `:162-176`), so register `pc == semantic-pc` for every `:call` instruction, with `segment-address = (rcode/register-hash r-image)`.\\n     - `derive/stack-image` ([`derive.cljc:60-120`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/derive.cljc#L60-L120)) walks each parsed `{:op :pc :children}` node and at `:call` (`:92-93`) emits `[:push]` for each child followed by `(emit! [:call (count y) z])`. At that `emit!`, the stack PC is `(count @image)` and the semantic PC is `(:pc node)`. `stack-image` already records `{:kind :closure :source pc}` and `{:kind :var :source pc}` in `:side-table` (`:79,88,90,120`).\\n   - **What fails if done carelessly**: Over 40 call sites across `src/` and `test/` (including [`linker/relowered`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc#L2131-L2132) and [`rcode/register-image-defect`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc#L699-L707)) pass `(derive/register-image v)` directly to `rcode/register-hash`, `rcode/register-image-defect`, and `rvm/create-vm`.\\n   - **Minimal boundary-respecting remedy**: Keep the return shapes of `(:image (derive/stack-image v))` and `(derive/register-image v)` byte-identical so existing hashes and lowering profiles (`linker/stack-lowering-profile`, `linker/register-lowering-profile`) are untouched. Record `:call` (and `:ffi-call`) `stack-pc -\\u003e semantic-pc` in `stack-image`'s `:side-table` (at [`derive.cljc:92-95`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/derive.cljc#L92-L95)) and add a pure helper in `derive.cljc` (e.g., `derive/instruction-provenance`) that composes semantic provenance `[[sem-addr sem-pc origin root path] ...]` with stack (`h` = `(dcode/image-hash h-image)`) and register (`r` = `(rcode/register-hash r-image)`) PC mappings to emit `[segment-address native-pc origin root-address path]`. Persist the instruction-provenance relations in [`publish-closure!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L356-L368) beside `:yang.call-site/table` (outside the closed schema-1 manifest hash, preserving `83b52a0b`).\\n\\n3. **[P1 — Path Shift Under `kernel-stamp-sites` in the Oracle Bridge] (`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2192-2320, 2449-2476`)**:\\n   - **What fails if unaddressed**: In [`kernel-compile`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj#L2460-L2465), `(yang/compile-program program true opts)` produces the unstamped C1-annotated map AST `compiled`. Then [`kernel-stamp-sites`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj#L2227-L2237) rewrites every stamped call's `args-node` into `(data/nth (dsg__intra_call gate-site! (conj [] k args-node)) 1)`. When a guest call is nested inside the arguments of an outer stamped guest call (`:2261, :2277`), the wrapper shifts the inner call's structural `path` in `stamped` relative to `compiled`, and adds 3 synthetic `:application` nodes (`data/nth`, `dsg__intra_call`, `conj`) per stamped site.\\n   - **Minimal boundary-respecting remedy**: During `kernel-stamp-sites` (or a paired walk over the unstamped `compiled` AST before/during stamping), track the exact grammar structural `path` (using `vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar` slot positions, matching [`linearize/slot-position`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc#L33-L43)) in the **unstamped** compiled tree (and, if stamping is retained for runtime execution, also in the C1-re-annotated `stamped` tree). Pass the unstamped C program through `encoder/program-batch` → `macro/expand-batch` (with explicit fixture admission origin) so every stamped integer site `k` (`1..N`) binds 1-to-1 to its canonical persisted occurrence key `K = [origin root-address path]` in the post-expansion C1 side table.\\n   - **Why evaluator runtime changes are NOT needed**: The oracle's guest-level `gate-site!` cell instrumentation ([`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:1983-2013`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj#L1983-L2013)) is explicitly licensed by Signed Addendum A §A1/§A3 ([`1794630000000:13,21`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794630000000-architect-attribution-addendum-a-RECORD.md#L13)) and Design §2.5/§4.1 ([`1794670000000:81-101, 219`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L81-L101)). It already captures the caller site after operand evaluation and before callee body entry in both `:c-walker` and `:c-semantic` within the 4,000,000-instruction budget. Binding integer `k` to persisted `K = [origin root-address path]` via `:yang.correspondence/origin-bindings` (`[[site-id K] ...]`) satisfies Design §2.5 and §4.2 (independent reconstruction, exact coverage of all `:application` occurrences including uncredited helpers, and exact multiplicities) while leaving `ast_walker`, `semantic`, `stack`, and `register` evaluators untouched for the continuation-semantics seat.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Question 2 — `D1` Evidence Format\\n\\n`Q2 VERDICT: (ii) SEPARATE COMPANION FILE test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_correspondence.edn REFERENCING VERBATIM :version 1 slice9_site_tables.edn.`\\n\\n### Evidence-Backed Reasoning\\n\\n1. **Compatibility Argument (Complete Grep of Readers \\u0026 Writers)**:\\n   - Across `src/`, `test/`, and `docs/`, [`test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_site_tables.edn`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_site_tables.edn) has **only one code reader** and **one code writer**:\\n     - Reader: [`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:3412-3415`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj#L3412-L3415) (`test-kernel-gate-evidence-writer-round-trip`), which asserts `(= 1 (:version tables))` and `(= (count (:fixtures written)) (count (:fixtures tables)))`.\\n     - Writer: [`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:3284-3293`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj#L3284-L3293) (`write-kernel-gate-evidence!`, plus temp-file cleanup at `:3418`).\\n     - Metadata pointer: [`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:3247`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj#L3247) and [`test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_evidence.edn:25`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_evidence.edn#L25) (`:site-tables-file \\\"slice9_site_tables.edn\\\"`).\\n     - Prose citations: [`test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_gate.md:24,228`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_gate.md#L24) and [`test/yang/latte_oracle/attribution_inventory.md:202`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle/attribution_inventory.md#L202).\\n   - However, **in-memory consumers** of `(:site-table row)` in `test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj` require homogeneous keys matching the third element of `:executed-calls` (`[fname arity site-id]` in `slice9_evidence.edn`):\\n     - [`kernel-stale-sites`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj#L2368-L2382) iterates `(for [[k s] table :when (and (symbol? (:callee s)) (not (contains? recorded k)))] k)` and calls `(sort ...)` at line 2380.\\n     - Under choice (i), dual-keying `:site-table` in-place with both integer keys (`1..N`) and vector keys (`K = [origin root-address path]`) while `:executed-calls` in `slice9_evidence.edn` records integer `1..N` causes **two immediate breakages**: (a) every `K` key is not in `recorded` and is falsely reported as a stale site, and (b) `(sort ...)` over mixed `java.lang.Long` and `PersistentVector` keys throws `ClassCastException`!\\n\\n2. **Failure-Mode \\u0026 Contract Argument (Design §1, §2.5, §3.4, §4.1, §4.2 and Unitarity)**:\\n   - **Design §1 (`1794670000000:12`)**: *\\\"Publish the durable correspondence as an additional addressable record referring to the oracle's evidence **without changing that evidence's format**.\\\"*\\n   - **Design §2.5 (`1794670000000:97`)**: *\\\"preserve its evidence verbatim and publish a reviewed binding of its origin fields to this semantic domain; **do not rewrite its tables behind an unchanged version**.\\\"*\\n   - **Design §4.1 (`1794670000000:183-220`)**: Defines `:yang.correspondence/schema 1` with a **closed key set** (`:200`), where `:yang.correspondence/evidence` points to `\\u003cJing address of OracleEvidence\\u003e` (\\\"**OracleEvidence verbatim**: same EDN data shape, schema/version, field names, vectors, site ids, source-hash value and classifications. Do not project a subset or copy its rows into a second durable site-table shape\\\", `:202`), and `:yang.correspondence/origin-bindings` (`[[\\u003cephemeral site id from OracleEvidence\\u003e \\u003cpersisted occurrence key\\u003e] ...]`, `:188-189, 219`) binds the oracle's integer site IDs to persisted C1 occurrence keys `K = [origin root-address path]`.\\n   - **Comment in `test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:3281-3283`**: *\\\"one derived table and one canonical-source-hash per fixture, stable across refreshes so the later durable correspondence record lands additively\\\"* — keeping `slice9_site_tables.edn` byte-stable while landing `slice9_correspondence.edn` beside it honors this comment literally and matches the `83b52a0b` (`:yang.call-site/schema 1` naming `:yang.call-site/manifest`) and `yang.python.antlr.siteset` (`siteset.cljc:5-22`) precedents cited in Design §4.2 (`:223`).\\n   - **Failure-mode separation (Design §3.4, `:171-174`)**: With a separate `slice9_correspondence.edn`, any corruption, recipe mismatch, or origin-binding failure in `D1` fails D1 correspondence verification cleanly without mutating or invalidating the accepted `:version 1` oracle evidence (`slice9_site_tables.edn` and `slice9_evidence.edn`), and never rewrites historical evidence.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Question 3 — Decomposition Confirmation\\n\\n`Q3 VERDICT: AMEND ORDER TO cc2 → cc3 → D1 → cc4 (D1 before cc4).`\\n\\n### Dependency Analysis \\u0026 Ordering Justification\\n\\n1. **Does `D1` depend on `cc4` (four-host equality + budget gate)? No.**\\n   - `D1` produces `test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_correspondence.edn`, the `:yang.correspondence.recipe/schema 1` recipe, and the 7-step independent reconstruction verifier ([`Design §4.2:225-235`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L225-L235)) in `test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj` / `src/dev/latte_oracle_tables.clj`.\\n   - The LaTTe oracle is JVM-only (`.clj`). Its prerequisites are `cc1` (landed), `cc2` (in flight on `cc2-transform-session-c1`), and `cc3` (lowering provenance in `linearize.cljc`/`derive.cljc`/`publish.cljc` + the oracle `site-id ↔ K` binding). Once `cc3` lands, `D1` has zero dependency on `cc4`'s Node, Dart, or Jolt host lanes.\\n\\n2. **Does `cc4` depend on `D1`? Yes — by both the signed acceptance sequence and the budget specification:**\\n   - **Design §8 Steps 3 → 4 → 5 (`1794670000000:373-375`) and Signed Addendum A §A4 (`1794630000000:25`)**:\\n     - Step 3 (`cc1`–`cc3`) implements common occurrence/side-table production, preservation, and publication.\\n     - Step 4 (`D1`) implements and independently reconstructs `D1` **before** Step 5 (`cc4`, accepting each production frontend after its four-host brief, cross-host equality, and budget measurements pass).\\n     - Signed Addendum A §A4 (`1794630000000:25`) explicitly strikes *\\\"or atomically with\\\"*: D1 implementation and independent verification must complete before accepting reliance.\\n   - **Design §5.3 (`1794670000000:284`) \\u0026 §6.1 (`1794670000000:296`)**:\\n     - Design §6.1 defines the mandatory static budget `S_static` (measured in `cc4`) to include *\\\"exact encoded bytes of C1 rows, provenance tables, retained origin records, **D1 and its reconstruction inputs**\\\"*, and Design §5.3 requires the frontend acceptance bundle (`cc4`) to include the completed D1 verification result. Running `D1` before `cc4` allows `cc4` to measure the final `D1` artifact bytes in `S_static` and include the D1 verification result in a single pass.\\n   - **Engineering Risk Reduction**:\\n     - Running `D1`'s 7-step independent reconstruction verifier immediately after `cc3` stress-tests `cc3`'s C1 side-table and instruction-provenance schemas on the full 54-fixture LaTTe corpus *before* running the expensive four-host (JVM, Node, Dart, Jolt) replay equality and prelude republication battery in `cc4`. If `D1` exposes any schema or provenance defect in `cc3`, fixing it before `cc4` avoids repeating the 4-host verification run.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Risks Surfaced to the Owner\\n\\n1. **Exception-Track (B)-Fallback Pre-Claim Hazard (`collab/exception-track/1794343000000-exception-track-surface-registry.md:32-36, 54-58`)**:\\n   - The continuation-semantics seat has noted a conditional `(B)` fallback if Clojure R4 equivalence proof fails, which could touch `clojure.cljc` broadly or pre-claim `encoder.cljc`, `publish.cljc`, `linearize.cljc`, or `derive.cljc`. Because `cc3` touches `linearize.cljc`, `derive.cljc`, and `publish.cljc`, dispatching `cc3` promptly after `cc2` lands (while Clojure R3/R4 is still in its `clojure.cljc`-internal phase) avoids any file-lock contention.\\n2. **Untracked vs. Tracked Code Size of `slice9_correspondence.edn` (`Design §6.1, §6.3`)**:\\n   - In `D1`, storing full C1 metadata rows and instruction-provenance tables inline for all 54 LaTTe fixtures inside a single checked-in EDN file could make `slice9_correspondence.edn` very large (tens of megabytes) because each fixture compiles the inlined LaTTe kernel + preludeclosure. To keep `slice9_correspondence.edn` compact and diffable while satisfying Design §4.1 (`:183-205`), `slice9_correspondence.edn` should store the **content addresses (`dao.jing` digests)** for `:yang.correspondence/evidence`, `:yang.correspondence/recipe`, `:yang.correspondence/metadata`, and `:yang.correspondence/instruction-provenance` alongside the compact `:yang.correspondence/origin-bindings` (`[[site-int K] ...]`) per fixture, and the 7-step verifier (`Design §4.2`) should reconstruct and verify those content-addressed relations in a content-addressed store/handle during verification rather than checking in multi-megabyte raw instruction vectors per fixture.\\n3. **Jolt J2 Load Check in `cc4` (`collab/jolt/1794900000000-orchestrator-handoff-jolt-seat.md:33-34`)**:\\n   - When `cc4` runs the four-host gate (JVM, Node, Dart, Jolt), ensure `yang.clojure-callsite-test` is wired into the Jolt lane alongside the pending J2 load check of `yang.clojure` so both obligations close in one Jolt run.\\n\",\"duration_seconds\":313.156519,\"num_turns\":1,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":165522,\"output_tokens\":21613,\"thinking_tokens\":12893,\"cache_read_tokens\":1086833,\"total_tokens\":187135}}\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793294621496-compiler-engineer-hardening2.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:9:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_3\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1,120p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj; sed -n '1350,1720p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj; cat src/dev/latte_oracle_tables.clj; cat test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_gate.md; head -35 test/yang/latte_oracle/manifest.edn; rg -n 'commit|format' docs/agents/format.md; sed -n '1820,2040p' src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"(ns yang.latte-oracle-test\\n  \\\"Pinned upstream LaTTe differential harness, slices 1-9 of the Yang gap\\n   program. A executes the original library on Clojure. B executes explicit\\n   portability source on Clojure; C compiles it through Yang for the walker\\n   and semantic VMs. Slice 9 fails closed on the full kernel corpus. The\\n   legacy classifier records historical blockers;\\n   the context module additionally checks free-symbol admission before C.\\n   Adaptations, operation sequences and scope departures live beside the\\n   manifest in yang/latte_oracle/.\\\"\\n  (:require [clojure.java.io :as io]\\n            [clojure.edn :as edn]\\n            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\\n            [clojure.string :as str]\\n            [clojure.walk :as walk]\\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\\n            [clojure.tools.reader :as r]\\n            [clojure.tools.reader.reader-types :as rt]\\n            [yang.clojure :as yang]\\n            [yang.clojure-test :as compiler-test]\\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\\n            [yin.vm.data :as data]\\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\\n            [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]\\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows-support :as rows-support]\\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]\\n            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\\n            [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as linearize]\\n            [yin.vm.ucf :as ucf]))\\n\\n\\n(def ^:private manifest\\n  (edn/read-string (slurp (io/resource \\\"yang/latte_oracle/manifest.edn\\\"))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- ns-declaration-aliases\\n  \\\"Alias -> full ns symbol, taken from the file's own (ns ...) declaration —\\n   never invented: ::alias/kw must read as :that.real.ns/kw.\\\"\\n  [ns-form]\\n  (let [alias-map (atom {})\\n        consume-spec (fn [spec]\\n                       (when (sequential? spec)\\n                         (let [lib (first spec)]\\n                           (loop [xs (rest spec)]\\n                             (when (seq xs)\\n                               (if (= :as (first xs))\\n                                 (do (swap! alias-map assoc (second xs) lib)\\n                                     (recur (drop 2 xs)))\\n                                 (recur (next xs))))))))]\\n    (loop [clauses (rest (rest ns-form))]\\n      (when (seq clauses)\\n        (let [clause (first clauses)]\\n          (if (and (seq? clause) (= :require (first clause)))\\n            (do (loop [reqs (next clause)]\\n                  (let [spec (first reqs)]\\n                    (when (and (not (nil? spec)) (not (keyword? spec)))\\n                      (consume-spec spec)\\n                      (recur (next reqs)))))\\n                (recur (next clauses)))\\n            (recur (next clauses))))))\\n    @alias-map))\\n\\n\\n(defn- read-forms\\n  \\\"Read one latte-kernel source file with reader conditionals resolved for\\n   :clj, ::alias/kw keywords resolved against the file's own ns declaration,\\n   and ::kw resolved against the file's own namespace — so the C leg compiles\\n   the same keyword identities the upstream A leg runs.\\\"\\n  [ns-sym]\\n  (let [f (io/resource (str (str/replace (name ns-sym) \\\".\\\" \\\"/\\\") \\\".cljc\\\"))\\n        pr (rt/source-logging-push-back-reader (java.io.PushbackReader. (io/reader f)) 1 (str f))]\\n    (let [ns-form (r/read {:read-cond :allow :features #{:clj} :eof ::eof} pr)\\n          declared-name (second ns-form)\\n          aliases (ns-declaration-aliases ns-form)]\\n      (binding [r/*alias-map* aliases\\n                *ns* (the-ns (create-ns declared-name))]\\n        (loop [acc []]\\n          (let [form (r/read {:read-cond :allow :features #{:clj} :eof ::eof} pr)]\\n            (if (= form ::eof) acc (recur (conj acc form)))))))))\\n\\n\\n(def ^:private all-forms\\n  (into {} (map (fn [ns-sym] [ns-sym (read-forms ns-sym)])\\n                (distinct (map :ns manifest)))))\\n\\n\\n(def ^:private top-forms\\n  (into {} (map (fn [{:keys [ns kind name]}]\\n                  [[ns name] (first (filter #(and (seq? %)\\n                                                  (= kind (first %))\\n                                                  (= name (second %)))\\n                                            (get all-forms ns)))]))\\n        manifest))\\n\\n\\n(def ^:private scanned-symbols\\n  #{'loop 'recur 'case 'throw 'ex-info 'atom 'swap! 'reset! 'lazy-seq 'gensym\\n    'apply 'comp 'partial 'reduced 'reduce 'map 'mapv 'filter 'remove 'into\\n    'concat 'merge 'str 'symbol 'keyword 'vector 'seq 'nth 'nthnext 'assoc-in\\n    'count 'name 'when-let 'if-let 'when-some 'if-some 'cond})\\n\\n\\n(defn- walk-symbols\\n  [form]\\n  (cond\\n    (seq? form) (if (and (= 'quote (first form)) (= 2 (count form)))\\n                  #{}\\n                  (mapcat walk-symbols form))\\n    (vector? form) (mapcat walk-symbols form)\\n    (map? form) (mapcat walk-symbols (concat (keys form) (vals form)))\\n    (set? form) (mapcat walk-symbols form)\\n    (symbol? form) (if (namespace form) #{} #{form})\\n    :else #{}))\\n\\n\\n(defn- destructuring?\\n  [binding]\\n  (not (symbol? binding)))\\n\\n\\n(def ^:private kernel-gate-corpus\\n  (edn/read-string (slurp (io/resource \\\"yang/latte_oracle/kernel_gate.edn\\\"))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- kernel-symbol [{:keys [ns name]}]\\n  (symbol (str/replace (str ns) \\\"_\\\" \\\"-\\\") (str name)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- kernel-guest-name [s]\\n  (symbol (str \\\"gate-\\\" (last (str/split (namespace s) #\\\"\\\\.\\\")) \\\"-\\\" (name s))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- kernel-arities [form]\\n  (when (#{'defn 'defn-} (first form))\\n    (let [header (drop-while #(not (or (vector? %) (seq? %))) (nnext form))\\n          params (if (vector? (first header)) [(first header)] (map first header))]\\n      (mapv (fn [p] (if (some #{'&} p) [:variadic (.indexOf p '&)] (count p))) params))))\\n\\n\\n(def ^:private kernel-entries\\n  (mapv (fn [entry]\\n          (let [s (kernel-symbol entry)]\\n            (upstream-fn s) ; load the real aliases and refers before resolving source\\n            (assoc entry :symbol s :arities (kernel-arities (get top-forms [(:ns entry) (:name entry)])))))\\n        manifest))\\n\\n\\n(defn- kernel-resolve [ns-sym s]\\n  (when (symbol? s)\\n    (let [n (the-ns (symbol (str/replace (str ns-sym) \\\"_\\\" \\\"-\\\")))\\n          v (ns-resolve n s)]\\n      (when (and (var? v) (str/starts-with? (str (:ns (meta v))) \\\"latte-kernel.\\\"))\\n        (symbol (str (:ns (meta v))) (str (:name (meta v))))))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- kernel-rewrite\\n  \\\"Resolve library names against their actual upstream namespace, respecting\\n   lexical binders and quote. No blanket alias stripping or data rewriting.\\\"\\n  [ns-sym form]\\n  (letfn [(bindings [pattern] (set (filter symbol? (tree-seq coll? seq pattern))))\\n          (forms [xs bound] (map #(step % bound) xs))\\n          (arity [xs bound]\\n            (let [[params & body] xs]\\n              (list* params (forms body (into bound (bindings params))))))\\n          (step [x bound]\\n            (cond\\n              (symbol? x) (cond\\n                            (contains? bound x) x\\n                            (#{\\\"set\\\" \\\"clojure.set\\\"} (namespace x)) (symbol (name x))\\n                            (= \\\"pp\\\" (namespace x)) (symbol \\\"clojure.pprint\\\" (name x))\\n                            (contains? '{get-in lookup-in not-empty context-not-empty\\n                                         ffirst context-ffirst list* context-list-star} x)\\n                            (get '{get-in lookup-in not-empty context-not-empty\\n                                   ffirst context-ffirst list* context-list-star} x)\\n                            :else (if-let [s (kernel-resolve ns-sym x)]\\n                                    ;; empty-env at the immutable-context boundary\\n                                    ;; is the same explicit initialization used by\\n                                    ;; the slice-8 fixtures, including default arities.\\n                                    (if (= s 'latte-kernel.defenv/empty-env)\\n                                      initial-context\\n                                      (if (and (= \\\"latte-kernel.defenv\\\" (namespace s))\\n                                               (str/starts-with? (name s) \\\"->\\\"))\\n                                        (symbol (name s)) (kernel-guest-name s))) x))\\n              (seq? x)\\n              (let [[op & xs] x]\\n                (cond\\n                  (= op 'quote) x\\n                  (and (= op 'lazy-seq) (= ns-sym 'latte_kernel.utils) (= 'zip (second form)))\\n                  (step (second x) bound)\\n                  (#{'fn 'fn*} op)\\n                  (cons 'fn (if (vector? (first xs)) (arity xs bound)\\n                                (map #(arity % bound) xs)))\\n                  (#{'let 'loop} op)\\n                  (let [[bs & body] xs\\n                        [bs' scope] (reduce (fn [[out scope] [p init]]\\n                                              [(conj out p (step init scope)) (into scope (bindings p))])\\n                                            [[] bound] (partition 2 bs))]\\n                    (list* op bs' (forms body scope)))\\n                  ;; The slice-8 delta boundary: both namespaces use one binding.\\n                  (and (#{'deref 'clojure.core/deref} op) (= xs '(+unfold-implicit+)))\\n                  '(:unfold-implicit def-env)\\n                  :else (apply list (forms x bound))))\\n              (vector? x) (mapv #(step % bound) x)\\n              (map? x) (into (empty x) (map (fn [[k v]] [(step k bound) (step v bound)])) x)\\n              (set? x) (into #{} (forms x bound))\\n              :else x))]\\n    (let [[kind fname & header] form\\n          header (drop-while #(not (or (vector? %) (seq? %))) header)\\n          guest (kernel-guest-name (kernel-symbol {:ns ns-sym :name fname}))]\\n      (if (#{'defn 'defn-} kind)\\n        (list* 'defn guest\\n               (if (vector? (first header)) (arity header #{}) (map #(arity % #{}) header)))\\n        (list 'def guest (step (nth form 2) #{}))))))\\n\\n\\n(def ^:private kernel-context-adapters\\n  ;; Reuse the established slice-8 representation boundary; no new compiler\\n  ;; workaround or truncated proof-step dispatcher is admitted here.\\n  '#{definition? theorem? axiom? notation? implicit? latte-definition?\\n     local-definitions register-definition fetch-definition registered-definition? qualify-def})\\n\\n\\n(defn- kernel-source [{:keys [ns name symbol arities]}]\\n  (cond\\n    (and (= ns 'latte_kernel.defenv) (contains? kernel-context-adapters name))\\n    (list* 'defn (kernel-guest-name symbol)\\n           (map (fn [n]\\n                  (let [ps (mapv #(clojure.core/symbol (str \\\"p\\\" %)) (range n))]\\n                    (list ps (list* name ps)))) arities))\\n    :else (kernel-rewrite ns (get top-forms [ns name]))))\\n\\n\\n(def ^:private kernel-sources\\n  (into {} (map (fn [entry] [(kernel-guest-name (:symbol entry)) (kernel-source entry)])) kernel-entries))\\n\\n\\n(defn- kernel-call [form]\\n  ;; Fixture code uses fully qualified names. Constructor adapters are the\\n  ;; five existing context constructors, outside the 143-binding manifest.\\n  (letfn [(rewrite [x]\\n            (cond\\n              (and (seq? x) (= 'quote (first x))) x\\n              (symbol? x) (if (and (namespace x) (str/starts-with? (namespace x) \\\"latte-kernel.\\\"))\\n                            (if (str/starts-with? (name x) \\\"->\\\") (symbol (name x)) (kernel-guest-name x)) x)\\n              (seq? x) (apply list (map rewrite x))\\n              (vector? x) (mapv rewrite x)\\n              (map? x) (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(rewrite k) (rewrite v)])) x)\\n              (set? x) (set (map rewrite x))\\n              :else x))]\\n    (rewrite form)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- kernel-closure [call]\\n  (let [sources (merge (into {} (map (juxt second identity)) context-forms) kernel-sources)\\n        mentions #(filter (set (keys sources)) (walk-symbols %))\\n        needed (loop [todo (seq (mentions call)) seen #{}]\\n                 (if-let [n (first todo)]\\n                   (if (contains? seen n) (recur (next todo) seen)\\n                       (recur (concat (next todo) (mentions (get sources n))) (conj seen n))) seen))\\n        ordered (concat context-forms (map #(get kernel-sources (kernel-guest-name (:symbol %))) kernel-entries))]\\n    (filterv #(contains? needed (second %)) ordered)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- kernel-fixture-call [{:keys [call definitions project-proof?]} guest?]\\n  (let [env (if guest? initial-context 'latte-kernel.defenv/empty-env)\\n        register (if guest? 'register-definition 'latte-kernel.defenv/register-definition)\\n        env (reduce (fn [env definition] (list register env (if guest? (kernel-call definition) definition))) env definitions)\\n        call (if guest? (kernel-call call) call)\\n        call (if project-proof?\\n               (list 'let ['r call] '(if (= :ok (first r)) [:ok (rest (second r))] r)) call)]\\n    (list 'let ['env env] call)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- evidence-data\\n  \\\"EDN evidence retains all portable values and metadata. Nonportable host\\n   payloads are explicit evidence, not accepted representation differences.\\\"\\n  [x]\\n  (cond\\n    (fn? x) {:nonportable-host-value (str (class x))}\\n    (record? x) (evidence-data (upstream-record-data x))\\n    (map? x) (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(evidence-data k) (evidence-data v)])) x)\\n    (vector? x) (mapv evidence-data x)\\n    (set? x) (set (map evidence-data x))\\n    (seq? x) (apply list (map evidence-data x))\\n    :else x))\\n\\n\\n(defn- kernel-attempt [f]\\n  (try (f)\\n       (catch Exception e\\n         {:status :blocked :message (ex-message e) :data (evidence-data (ex-data e))\\n          :causes (mapv (fn [cause] {:class (str (class cause)) :message (ex-message cause)})\\n                        (take-while some? (iterate ex-cause e)))\\n          :exception (str (class e))})))\\n\\n\\n(defn- kernel-a [fixture]\\n  (kernel-attempt\\n    #(let [value (if (= :unparser (:mode fixture))\\n                   (with-redefs-fn {(upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.unparser/+unparser-registry+)\\n                                   (atom {:fundamental [] :standard [] :user [] :unparsers {}})}\\n                     (fn []\\n                       ((upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.unparser/register-unparser!) :gate (eval (:extension fixture)))\\n                       (a-leg (upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.unparser/unparse) [(:term fixture)])))\\n                   (a-leg (eval (list 'fn [] (kernel-fixture-call fixture false))) []))]\\n       {:status :completed :outcome (evidence-data value) :shape (result-shape (evidence-data value))})))\\n\\n\\n(defn- kernel-c-program [fixture]\\n  (if (= :unparser (:mode fixture))\\n    (list 'unparse (list 'register-unparser initial-context :gate (:extension fixture)) (list 'quote (:term fixture)))\\n    (kernel-fixture-call fixture true)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- kernel-b [fixture]\\n  (kernel-attempt\\n    #(let [sandbox (create-ns (gensym \\\"kernel-gate-b-\\\"))\\n           call (kernel-c-program fixture)\\n           forms (kernel-closure call)\\n           host-form (fn [form]\\n                       ;; Preserve the actual one-argument gensym call. Only\\n                       ;; the slice-8 explicit two-argument supply is adapted.\\n                       (walk/postwalk\\n                         (fn [x]\\n                           (if (and (seq? x) (= 'gensym (first x)) (= 2 (count x)))\\n                             (cons 'clojure.core/gensym (rest x)) x)) form))]\\n       (try\\n         (binding [*ns* sandbox]\\n           (refer 'clojure.core)\\n           (require '[clojure.set :refer [union difference]])\\n           (eval (list* 'declare\\n                        (concat (map second forms)\\n                                (for [[ns-sym source] all-forms\\n                                      form source :when (= 'declare (first form))\\n                                      s (rest form)\\n                                      :let [qualified (kernel-resolve ns-sym s)]\\n                                      :when qualified]\\n                                  (kernel-guest-name qualified)))))\\n           (doseq [form forms] (eval (context-host-form (host-form form))))\\n           (let [v (a-leg (eval (list 'fn [] (context-host-form (host-form call)))) [])]\\n             {:status :completed :outcome (evidence-data v) :shape (result-shape (evidence-data v))}))\\n         (finally (remove-ns (ns-name sandbox)))))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- kernel-compile [fixture]\\n  (let [call (kernel-c-program fixture)\\n        forms (kernel-closure call)\\n        program (conj forms call)\\n        program (into (yang/library-for program) program)\\n        ast (yang/compile-program program true arg-vector-opts)\\n        missing (unbound-ast-symbols ast program)]\\n    (if (seq missing)\\n      {:status :blocked :phase :admission :blocked-by (vec (sort missing))\\n       :owners (into {} (for [s missing]\\n                         [s (mapv second (filter #(some #{s} (tree-seq coll? seq %)) program))]))}\\n      {:status :compiled :ast ast :forms forms})))\\n\\n\\n(defn- kernel-c [compiled lane]\\n  (if (= :compiled (:status compiled))\\n    (assoc (kernel-attempt\\n             #(let [v (compiler-test/run-guest-ast (:ast compiled) (oracle-registry yang/kind-module) lane 1000000)]\\n                {:status :completed :outcome (evidence-data v) :shape (result-shape (evidence-data v))}))\\n           :lane lane)\\n    (assoc compiled :lane lane)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- kernel-row [fixture]\\n  (let [a (kernel-a fixture)\\n        b (kernel-b fixture)\\n        compiled (kernel-attempt #(kernel-compile fixture))\\n        compiled (if (and (= :blocked (:status compiled)) (not (:blocked-by compiled)))\\n                   (assoc compiled :phase :compile\\n                          :blocked-by (if-let [n (get-in compiled [:data :name])] [n] [:compiler-exception])\\n                          :minimal-source (get kernel-sources (get-in compiled [:data :name]))) compiled)\\n        walker (kernel-c compiled :walker)\\n        semantic (kernel-c compiled :semantic)\\n        match? (and (= :completed (:status a) (:status b) (:status walker) (:status semantic))\\n                    (= (:outcome a) (:outcome b))\\n                    (agrees? (get a :outcome) (get walker :outcome))\\n                    (= (:outcome walker) (:outcome semantic))\\n                    (= (result-shape (:outcome a)) (result-shape (:outcome b)))\\n                    (if (contains? (:outcome a) :value)\\n                      (= (result-shape (:value (:outcome a)))\\n                         (result-shape (second (:outcome walker))))\\n                      (= (result-shape (get-in a [:outcome :thrown :data]))\\n                         (result-shape (get-in walker [:outcome 1 :yin.k/data])))))\\n        status (cond match? :pass\\n                     (some #(= :blocked (:status %)) [a b walker semantic]) :blocked\\n                     :else :mismatch)]\\n    {:id (:id fixture) :negative? (boolean (:negative? fixture)) :status status\\n     :dependency-of (:dependency-of fixture)\\n     :call (or (:call fixture) (kernel-c-program fixture))\\n     :a a :b b :c-walker walker :c-semantic semantic\\n     :included-functions (mapv second (kernel-closure (kernel-c-program fixture)))}))\\n\\n\\n(defn kernel-gate-evidence\\n  \\\"Run every fixture in A and independently in both C lanes. Compilation or\\n   VM errors are blockers, never successful LaTTe rejections. Source closure\\n   membership is recorded separately from conservative execution coverage.\\\"\\n  []\\n  (let [results (mapv kernel-row (:fixtures kernel-gate-corpus))\\n        inventory (mapv #(select-keys % [:symbol :kind :arities]) kernel-entries)\\n        ;; Direct calls are a lower bound, not a claim that every function in\\n        ;; a dependency closure was executed. Unproven transitive arities stay\\n        ;; unexercised and block closure of the gate.\\n        direct (into #{}\\n                     (for [[fixture row] (map vector (:fixtures kernel-gate-corpus) results)\\n                           :when (= :pass (:status row))\\n                           :let [call (:call fixture)]\\n                           :when (and (seq? call) (namespace (first call)))]\\n                       [(first call) (count (rest call))]))\\n        all-arities (set (for [{:keys [symbol arities]} inventory n arities] [symbol n]))\\n        unexercised (vec (sort-by pr-str (remove direct all-arities)))]\\n    {:slice 9 :gate-status (if (and (every? #(= :pass (:status %)) results) (empty? unexercised)) :pass :blocked)\\n     :generated-at (str (java.time.Instant/now))\\n     :adaptation-version {:context 1 :kernel-assembly 1}\\n     :executions {:a :original-upstream-clojure :b :context-source-clojure\\n                  :c [:walker :semantic]}\\n     :upstream-revision \\\"86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279\\\"\\n     :compiler-vm-revision \\\"f74f2cecccfc54813671555b15e39d254debd2d9\\\"\\n     :runtime {:clojure (clojure-version) :java (System/getProperty \\\"java.version\\\")}\\n     :instruction-budget-per-lane 1000000\\n     :manifest-bindings (count manifest) :function-arity-candidates (count all-arities)\\n     :manifest-functions (count (filter :arities kernel-entries))\\n     :admitted-function-arity-count :not-recorded-in-inherited-manifest\\n     :admission-note \\\"The inherited manifest has no admitted/excluded dispositions or arities. All function arities are conservatively retained as gate obligations; no narrowing by fixture success.\\\"\\n     :coverage {:proven-direct-function-arities (vec (sort-by pr-str direct))\\n                :exercised-count (count direct) :unexercised unexercised\\n                :transitive-execution-coverage :unproven\\n                :inventory inventory}\\n     :counts (frequencies (map :status results)) :fixture-count (count results)\\n     :negative-fixture-count (count (filter :negative? results))\\n     :dependency-graph\\n     (into (sorted-map)\\n           (for [[fname source] kernel-sources]\\n             [fname (vec (sort (filter (set (keys kernel-sources)) (walk-symbols source))))]))\\n     :fixtures results}))\\n\\n\\n(defn write-kernel-gate-evidence!\\n  \\\"Explicit evidence refresh; normal test runs never update the checked-in oracle.\\\"\\n  []\\n  (let [evidence (kernel-gate-evidence)]\\n    (with-open [w (io/writer \\\"test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_evidence.edn\\\")]\\n      ;; prn keeps (quote ...) in valid EDN rather than pprint's reader\\n      ;; shorthand. One fixture per line keeps refreshes independently diffable.\\n      (binding [*out* w *print-length* nil *print-level* nil]\\n        (print \\\"{\\\")\\n        (doseq [[k v] (dissoc evidence :fixtures)] (pr k) (print \\\" \\\") (prn v))\\n        (println \\\":fixtures [\\\")\\n        (doseq [row (:fixtures evidence)] (prn row))\\n        (println \\\"]}\\\")))\\n    (select-keys evidence [:gate-status :counts :fixture-count :manifest-bindings :function-arity-candidates :coverage])))\\n\\n\\n(deftest test-kernel-differential-gate\\n  (let [evidence (kernel-gate-evidence)]\\n    (is (= (count (:fixtures kernel-gate-corpus)) (count (set (map :id (:fixtures evidence)))))\\n        \\\"Every named fixture runs exactly once, including negatives\\\")\\n    (doseq [row (:fixtures evidence)\\n            :when (and (:negative? row) (= :completed (get-in row [:a :status])))\\n            :let [outcome (get-in row [:a :outcome]) value (:value outcome)]]\\n      (is (or (:thrown outcome) (false? value) (and (sequential? value) (= :ko (first value))))\\n          (str \\\"A must actually reject the named negative: \\\" (:id row))))\\n    (println \\\"KERNEL-GATE\\\" (pr-str (select-keys evidence [:gate-status :counts :fixture-count :manifest-bindings :function-arity-candidates])))\\n    (doseq [row (:fixtures evidence) :when (not= :pass (:status row))]\\n      (println \\\"KERNEL-BLOCKER\\\"\\n               (pr-str {:id (:id row) :status (:status row)\\n                        :blocked-by (get-in row [:c-walker :blocked-by])\\n                        :a (get-in row [:a :status]) :b (get-in row [:b :status])\\n                        :c-walker (get-in row [:c-walker :status])\\n                        :c-semantic (get-in row [:c-semantic :status])})))\\n    (is (= :pass (:gate-status evidence))\\n        (str \\\"Kernel gate remains blocked: \\\" (:counts evidence)\\n             \\\"; admitted/candidate but unexercised function/arities=\\\" (count (get-in evidence [:coverage :unexercised]))\\n             \\\". See slice9_evidence.edn; blocked fixtures are not accepted negatives.\\\"))))\\n;; Regenerate the LaTTe oracle's derived tables from the manifest forms:\\n;;   test/yang/latte_oracle/throw_sites.edn  (the throw-site inventory)\\n;;   test/yang/latte_oracle/case_arms.edn    (the per-arm case fixtures)\\n;; Both are derived by yang.latte-oracle-test, so this script and the test\\n;; cannot disagree about what a regenerated table holds.\\n;; Run: clj -X:test:dev latte-oracle-tables/-main\\n(ns latte-oracle-tables\\n  (:require [clojure.java.io :as io]\\n            [clojure.pprint :as pp]\\n            [yang.latte-oracle-test]))\\n\\n\\n(defn- derived\\n  \\\"The result of calling the oracle test's private derivation `sym`.\\\"\\n  [sym]\\n  ((deref (ns-resolve 'yang.latte-oracle-test sym))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- write-table!\\n  [file header rows]\\n  (io/make-parents file)\\n  (spit file (str header (with-out-str (pp/pprint rows))))\\n  (println \\\"wrote\\\" (count rows) \\\"rows to\\\" file))\\n\\n\\n(defn -main\\n  [& _]\\n  (write-table! \\\"test/yang/latte_oracle/throw_sites.edn\\\"\\n                (str \\\";; GENERATED from the manifest forms by yang.latte-oracle-test/throw-site-rows.\\\\n\\\"\\n                     \\\";; One row per throw symbol; disposition :fixture | :deferred | :excluded.\\\\n\\\")\\n                (derived 'throw-site-rows))\\n  (write-table! \\\"test/yang/latte_oracle/case_arms.edn\\\"\\n                (str \\\";; GENERATED from the manifest forms by yang.latte-oracle-test/case-arm-rows.\\\\n\\\"\\n                     \\\";; One row per case site: each arm's clause constants, and whether it has a default.\\\\n\\\")\\n                (derived 'case-arm-rows))\\n  (shutdown-agents))\\n# Slice 9 kernel differential gate — BLOCKED\\n\\nThis is a failing close-out gate, not a conformance certificate. No compiler or\\nVM source was changed. No commit was made.\\n\\nThe 54 fixtures in `kernel_gate.edn` invoke actual pinned upstream functions on A,\\nexecute the explicit context source on host Clojure on B, and compile the guest\\nsource for C-walker and C-semantic. Guest extension closures are evaluated by the\\nVM; the harness supplies no host callback primitive. The original proof dispatcher\\nis assembled, rather than substituting slice 8's restricted state-step dispatcher.\\nEvery fixture, including every negative, has an A/B/C-walker/C-semantic outcome in\\n`slice9_evidence.edn`. Blocked fixtures are attempted and recorded independently;\\nno negative is skipped or counted as a successful guest rejection.\\n\\nResult: **4 passing fixtures, 2 mismatches, 48 blocked fixtures**. Passing fixtures\\nare `:subst-capture`, `:subst-shadow`, `:subst-three-arity`, and\\n`:unparser-guest-closure`. The compile/admission blockers occur before either C\\nlane executes those blocked programs; both lane records explicitly say so.\\n\\n## Mismatches with minimal repros\\n\\n1. `:minimal-gensym-freshness`:\\n\\n   ```clojure\\n   (let [a (gensym \\\"fresh\\\") b (gensym \\\"fresh\\\")] (= a b))\\n   ```\\n\\n   A and B return `false`; both C lanes return `[:yin.k/ok true]`. The guest\\n   library's one-argument `gensym` constructs `G__fresh` repeatedly. This\\n   dependency is reachable from