om\\n  initialized with a closure. Yang rejects this `def` initializer under the\\n  outcome convention. Each affected fixture records\\n  `:blocked-by [gate-proof-+opacity-fn+]` and the exact `:minimal-source`.\\n  The inherited partial proof-step context adapter cannot stand in for the real\\n  parsing/typing dispatcher. Proof compilation separately reaches the missing\\n  `string?` dependency; even `:compile-proof`'s single `:qed` script is explicitly\\n  blocked by this dependency rather than treated as a successful rejection.\\n- Upstream's error for steps after `qed` includes the host `clojure.core/meta`\\n  function in its `:meta` field. Evidence explicitly marks this nonportable host\\n  value; it is not normalized into an accepted portability difference. The\\n  malformed scalar proof-step fixture also records its native upstream exception.\\n\\nThe complete source dependency graph, per-fixture closure membership, missing\\nsymbols and their owning definitions, compiler exception causes, and minimal\\ncalls are retained in `slice9_evidence.edn`. Compiler/admission/VM exceptions are\\nblockers; only actual returned `:ko`, `false`, or corresponding domain exceptions\\ncan satisfy negative fixtures. A test assertion checks that every completed A\\nnegative really rejects its input.\\n\\n## Manifest and coverage\\n\\nThe inherited manifest contains **155 bindings, 147 functions, and 175\\nfunction/arity entries**,\\nnot the plan's earlier estimate of 143 definitions. It has no admitted/excluded\\ndispositions, and its source fields are nil. Consequently an exact admitted\\nfunction/arity denominator cannot be recovered honestly from that manifest.\\n`admitted-function-arity-count` is explicitly `:not-recorded-in-inherited-manifest`.\\nAll 175 entries are retained as gate obligations; successful fixtures do not\\nnarrow the denominator.\\n\\nThe conservative, proven direct A/B/C agreement count is **2/175 arities**:\\n`latte-kernel.syntax/subst` at arities 2 and 3. The successful unparser integration\\nalso executes its dependencies, but this harness does not claim an exact dynamic\\ntransitive arity count. It records `:transitive-execution-coverage :unproven`.\\nAll **173 remaining unexercised-or-unproven entries** are individually listed\\nunder `:coverage :unexercised`, alongside the complete function/arity inventory.\\nDependency closure membership is recorded separately and does not count as\\nexecution. This incomplete accounting itself blocks the close-out gate.\\n\\n## Reproduction and verification\\n\\nPins: upstream LaTTe `86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279`; compiler/VM\\n`f74f2cecccfc54813671555b15e39d254debd2d9`; context adaptation v1, kernel assembly v1.\\nThe recorded host uses Clojure 1.12.4 and Java 17.0.18. Each C execution has a\\n1,000,000-instruction budget. There is no continuation-depth claim for blocked\\nprograms.\\n\\nRun the gate:\\n\\n```sh\\nclj -M:test -n yang.latte-oracle-test\\n```\\n\\n**22 tests, 988 assertions, 1 failure, 0 errors, exit 1.** The single failed\\nassertion is `test-kernel-differential-gate`: the gate must remain red while the\\nabove blockers or unproven coverage remain. The inherited 21 tests passed in the\\nbaseline: 968 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors. Do not remove the close-out\\nassertion to manufacture the requested zero-failure result.\\n\\nExplicitly refresh evidence from fresh A/B/C runs (normal test runs do not rewrite\\nit):\\n\\n```sh\\nclj -Sdeps '{:aliases {:gate {:main-opts [\\\"-e\\\" \\\"(require (quote yang.latte-oracle-test)) (println (select-keys (yang.latte-oracle-test/write-kernel-gate-evidence!) [:gate-status :counts :fixture-count :manifest-bindings :function-arity-candidates]))\\\"]}}}' -M:test:gate\\n```\\n\\nThis evidence-writing command returns normally even when the recorded gate is\\nblocked; only the test command above is the acceptance gate.\\n\\nUnchanged regression suites:\\n\\n```sh\\nclj -M:test -n yang.clojure-test -n yin.vm.macro-test -n yang.clojure.stream-eval-test -n yin.vm.store-write-audit-test\\n```\\n\\n**Blocked at namespace loading**, `ClassNotFoundException:\\nyang.python.antlr.gen.Python3Lexer`; no green four-suite result. The stream/REPL\\nsuite imports the frontend catalog that requires the generated Python parser.\\nThe prerequisite attempt\\n`clj -M:antlr-gen --grammar python3 --target java` failed with\\n`java.nio.channels.UnresolvedAddressException` while retrieving required inputs.\\n\\nThe independent suites were then run separately:\\n\\n```sh\\nclj -M:test -n yang.clojure-test -n yin.vm.macro-test -n yin.vm.store-write-audit-test\\nclj -M:test -n yin.vm.semantic.linearize-test -n yin.vm.semantic.analysis-test -n yin.vm.semantic.frame-test\\n```\\n\\nRespectively **106 tests / 1,007 assertions** and **45 tests / 1,944 assertions**,\\nboth with **0 failures and 0 errors**.\\n\\nCross-host regression availability is separate from the JVM kernel oracle:\\n\\n- `bb test:changed:cljs --changed test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj test/yang/latte_oracle/kernel_gate.edn`\\n  could not start: `bb` is absent (exit 127).\\n- Fallback `clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile test` failed before any\\n  Node tests ran. `CompilerOptions` requires class-file version 65 (Java 21), but\\n  the active runtime supports version 61 (Java 17). Node itself is available.\\n- Dart/Flutter are absent from PATH. No Dart suite ran; that lane is unavailable,\\n  not green. Four-evaluator stream/REPL verification remains blocked as above.\\n- `git diff --check` passed.\\n;; GENERATED by src/dev/latte_oracle_manifest.clj from the pinned\\n;; latte-kernel git dependency (deps.edn :test, sha 86fca0d1).\\n;; {:ns ... :kind defn|def|defn- :name ...} one entry per top-level binding.\\n[{:ns latte_kernel.defenv, :kind defn, :name definition?, :source nil}\\n {:ns latte_kernel.defenv, :kind def, :name empty-env, :source nil}\\n {:ns latte_kernel.defenv, :kind defn, :name mkenv, :source nil}\\n {:ns latte_kernel.defenv,\\n  :kind defn,\\n  :name local-definitions,\\n  :source nil}\\n {:ns latte_kernel.defenv,\\n  :kind defn,\\n  :name register-definition,\\n  :source nil}\\n {:ns latte_kernel.defenv,\\n  :kind defn,\\n  :name fetch-definition,\\n  :source nil}\\n {:ns latte_kernel.defenv,\\n  :kind defn,\\n  :name registered-definition?,\\n  :source nil}\\n {:ns latte_kernel.defenv, :kind defn, :name qualify-def, :source nil}\\n {:ns latte_kernel.defenv, :kind defn, :name theorem?, :source nil}\\n {:ns latte_kernel.defenv, :kind defn, :name axiom?, :source nil}\\n {:ns latte_kernel.defenv, :kind defn, :name notation?, :source nil}\\n {:ns latte_kernel.defenv, :kind defn, :name implicit?, :source nil}\\n {:ns latte_kernel.defenv,\\n  :kind defn,\\n  :name latte-definition?,\\n  :source nil}\\n {:ns latte_kernel.nbe, :kind defn, :name instantiate-def, :source nil}\\n {:ns latte_kernel.nbe,\\n  :kind def,\\n  :name +unfold-implicit+,\\n2:description: File and content format rules for datom.world — .chp/.blog EDN+Hiccup files, tables in .md files, and git commit message format\\n53:The example table above is itself in the format: `docs/agents/team.md` and\\n54:`docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md` are the reference\\n59:## Git commit messages\\n71:commits are exempt from this format. Never add `Co-Authored-By`, including\\n72:LLM attribution, to any commit in this repository.\\n74:Whether and when a commit is *allowed* to happen (review requirements,\\n75:authorization, undoing an unauthorized commit) is role-specific policy, not\\n76:format — see [`roles/orchestrator.md`](roles/orchestrator.md)'s Coordination\\n;; and a closure's failure ends the library function with the same outcome.\\n;;\\n;; What is derived, from the VM primitives and the `data` module only:\\n;; identity, inc/dec, second, the collection predicates (coll?/vector?/map?/\\n;; set?/seq?/list?/sequential?, from the `portable/*` adapters of data/count,\\n;; peek, dissoc and disj: a refusal as data says \\\"not that kind\\\"), boolean?,\\n;; fn? (data/callable?), seq, rem, reverse, list, cons, vector, count,\\n;; contains?, rest, map/mapv/filter/remove/reduce (with reduced)/into/concat/merge,\\n;; keys/vals/disj and set union/difference,\\n;; comp, partial, gensym (explicit supply), not=, and `apply`, which is a\\n;; compiler intrinsic over the convention's argument vector.\\n;;\\n;; What stays a host primitive, named by the `kind` module: a symbol, a\\n;; keyword and a host string are distinguished or built only by the host\\n;; (symbol?, keyword?, name, symbol, keyword, str, int?), as is metadata access\\n;; (meta). No `data` export or\\n;; VM primitive tells a symbol from a keyword. var? and resolve are the host's\\n;; Var primitives: a harness on a host with Vars registers them in `kind`\\n;; (`kind-module` leaves them out); a program that never mentions them does\\n;; not need them.\\n;;\\n;; Known compromises: `reduced` is an untyped tagged map, so reduced? matches\\n;; any map holding :yin.k/reduced true; seq refuses a non-collection (a string\\n;; is the data module's str-* ops, not a seq); eager sequences are lists;\\n;; rem rejects non-integers and a zero divisor before arithmetic; the compiler\\n;; emits bare conj and vec, so a program may not define or bind either.\\n;;\\n;; Variadic Clojure functions are fixed-arity here (the convention has no\\n;; variadic parameter): str, list and vector admit 0 to 6 arguments, concat and\\n;; merge 0 to 4, union 0 to 6, difference 2, comp 0 to 3, partial binds 1 to 3.\\n;; A larger count is the\\n;; function's own arity error.\\n\\n(def library-adapters\\n  \\\"The `:adapters` a program using `library` is compiled with: the data\\n   exports whose refusal the predicates read as data. The harness registers\\n   `portable/<name>` as `outcome-adapter` over the same `data/<name>`.\\\"\\n  {'data/count 'portable/count\\n   'data/peek 'portable/peek\\n   'data/dissoc 'portable/dissoc\\n   'data/disj 'portable/disj})\\n\\n\\n(def kind-module\\n  \\\"The `kind` host module's exports, symbol to host function: the irreducible\\n   kind and name primitives (see the library notes). Every export is pure.\\\"\\n  {'symbol? symbol?\\n   'keyword? keyword?\\n   'name name\\n   'symbol symbol\\n   'keyword keyword\\n   'str str\\n   'int? int?\\n   'meta meta})\\n\\n\\n(def kind-arities\\n  \\\"The published arities of each `kind` export.\\\"\\n  {'symbol? [1], 'keyword? [1], 'name [1], 'symbol [1 2], 'keyword [1 2]\\n   'str [0 1 2 3 4 5 6 :variadic], 'int? [1], 'meta [1]})\\n\\n\\n(def library\\n  \\\"The library's definitions, in order, as quoted source.\\\"\\n  '[(defn identity\\n      [x]\\n      x)\\n    (defn inc\\n      [x]\\n      (+ x 1))\\n    (defn dec\\n      [x]\\n      (- x 1))\\n    (defn second\\n      [x]\\n      (first (rest x)))\\n    (defn not=\\n      [a b]\\n      (not (= a b)))\\n    (defn boolean?\\n      [x]\\n      (or (= x true) (= x false)))\\n    (defn fn?\\n      [x]\\n      (data/callable? x))\\n    (defn count\\n      [x]\\n      (data/count x))\\n    (defn contains?\\n      [coll k]\\n      (data/contains? coll k))\\n    (defn symbol?\\n      [x]\\n      (kind/symbol? x))\\n    (defn keyword?\\n      [x]\\n      (kind/keyword? x))\\n    (defn int?\\n      [x]\\n      (kind/int? x))\\n    (defn meta\\n      [x]\\n      (kind/meta x))\\n    (defn name\\n      [x]\\n      (kind/name x))\\n    (defn var?\\n      [x]\\n      (kind/var? x))\\n    (defn resolve\\n      [x]\\n      (kind/resolve x))\\n    (defn symbol\\n      ([n] (kind/symbol n))\\n      ([ns n] (kind/symbol ns n)))\\n    (defn keyword\\n      ([n] (kind/keyword n))\\n      ([ns n] (kind/keyword ns n)))\\n    (defn str\\n      ([] \\\"\\\")\\n      ([a] (kind/str a))\\n      ([a b] (kind/str a b))\\n      ([a b c] (kind/str a b c))\\n      ([a b c d] (kind/str a b c d))\\n      ([a b c d e] (kind/str a b c d e))\\n      ([a b c d e f] (kind/str a b c d e f)))\\n    (defn gensym\\n      ([n] (kind/symbol (kind/str \\\"G__\\\" n)))\\n      ([prefix n] (kind/symbol (kind/str prefix n))))\\n    (defn coll?\\n      [x]\\n      (if (nil? x)\\n        false\\n        (= :yin.k/ok (first (yin.k/outcome-of (data/count x))))))\\n    (defn vector?\\n      [x]\\n      (if (nil? x)\\n        false\\n        (= :yin.k/ok (first (yin.k/outcome-of (data/peek x))))))\\n    (defn map?\\n      [x]\\n      (if (nil? x)\\n        false\\n        (= :yin.k/ok (first (yin.k/outcome-of (data/dissoc x))))))\\n    (defn set?\\n      [x]\\n      (if (nil? x)\\n        false\\n        (= :yin.k/ok (first (yin.k/outcome-of (data/disj x))))))\\n    (defn sequential?\\n      [x]\\n      (if (coll? x) (if (map? x) false (not (set? x))) false))\\n    (defn seq?\\n      [x]\\n      (if (sequential? x) (not (vector? x)) false))\\n    (defn list?\\n      [x]\\n      (seq? x))\\n    ;; The VM's rest returns a vector. Supply the source language's sequence\\n    ;; shape here without changing that VM primitive.\\n    (defn rest\\n      [coll]\\n      (let [v (vec coll)]\\n        (loop [i (- (count v) 1), acc '()]\\n          (if (< i 1) acc (recur (- i 1) (conj acc (data/nth v i)))))))\\n    (defn seq\\n      [x]\\n      (cond\\n        (nil? x) nil\\n        (if (coll? x) (empty? x) false) nil\\n        (seq? x) x\\n        (coll? x) (reverse (reverse x))\\n        :else (throw (ex-info \\\"seq of a non-collection is not supported\\\"\\n                              {:value x}))))\\n    (defn rem\\n      [a b]\\n      (cond\\n        (not (if (int? a) (int? b) false))\\n        (throw (ex-info \\\"rem requires integer operands\\\" {:a a :b b}))\\n        (= b 0) (throw (ex-info \\\"Divide by zero\\\" {:a a}))\\n        (< a 0) (- 0 (rem (- 0 a) b))\\n        (< b 0) (rem a (- 0 b))\\n        :else (loop [r a]\\n                (if (< r b) r (recur (- r b))))))\\n    (defn reverse\\n      [coll]\\n      (loop [s coll\\n             acc '()]\\n        (if (empty? s) acc (recur (rest