ding-text pending)))))\\n      (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) error\\n        (let [[st text] (drain-output state)\\n              d (ex-data error)]\\n          ;; retention evidence rides the shell-owned session state\\n          ;; (r11): st carries every handle and failure the parked\\n          ;; run's loaders recorded before it parked, so no exception\\n          ;; payload is read here -- a late throw from the resumed\\n          ;; run, its renderer or its result formatting cannot\\n          ;; fabricate handles, diagnostics or a Warning\\n          (fold-queued\\n            [(carry-served (assoc st\\n                                  :vm (query/discard-answers\\n                                        (carry-link-identity\\n                                          (:base parked)\\n                                          {:id-counter (::link-counter d)\\n                                           :origins (::link-origins d)})\\n                                        (:query-pair st))\\n                                  :pending-run nil)\\n                           d)\\n             (str text\\n                  (format-error error)\\n                  (dropped-lines-text (count (:pending-lines parked))))]\\n            (cond-> [] input (conj input))))))))\\n\\n\\n(defn recheck-pending\\n  \\\"One re-check of the shell's `:pending-run` without an input line --\\n   the step an unattended host drives at its own cadence\\n   (yin.repl.link-policy.md section 4): serve the interpreter, run the\\n   parked VM, and consult the link policy when the run is still\\n   pending.  A re-check that completes the run folds the retained lines\\n   exactly as a typed line's completion does.  Returns `[state text]`,\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793956400000-reviewer-h3-6-audit-verification.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:20:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_9\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '2350,2565p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj && sed -n '2630,2860p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"                                     (or (not= :ambient-delegation kind)\\n                                         (= :ambient-literal (first (:arg-shapes site-row)))))))\\n                            (get kernel-ambient-correspondence [symbol n])))))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- kernel-ambient-site?\\n  \\\"R2b case 5's compile-time verification, one site at a time: a site\\n   may claim the ambient correspondence only when the derived table says\\n   its compiled context argument (position 0) IS the adapter-supplied\\n   ambient literal and the site is not a self-delegation. A declaration\\n   naming any other site refuses.\\\"\\n  [table site-id]\\n  (let [site-row (get table site-id)]\\n    (and site-row\\n         (not (:delegation? site-row))\\n         (= :ambient-literal (first (:arg-shapes site-row))))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- kernel-stale-sites\\n  \\\"R2b case 8's diagnostic: site ids the declared table carries that no\\n   lane's trace ever records — a stale table after a fixture edit. The\\n   result is recorded data (never silent non-credit): only sites the\\n   attribution could have consulted (direct sites of instrumented\\n   callees) participate.\\\"\\n  [table lanes]\\n  (let [recorded (into #{}\\n                       (comp (mapcat #(get-in lanes [% :executed-calls]))\\n                             (filter vector?)\\n                             (map #(nth % 2 nil)))\\n                       [:c-walker :c-semantic])]\\n    (vec (sort (for [[k s] table\\n                     :when (and (symbol? (:callee s)) (not (contains? recorded k)))]\\n                 k)))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- kernel-executed-arity?\\n  \\\"The ruled attribution query over `row`'s two caller-site-tagged C-lane\\n   traces: upstream `symbol` at arity `n` is credited when BOTH lanes\\n   record a body entry the query admits (kernel-record