ss passed), and indexed `__all__` (range, generator/set/dict TypeErrors). Review: codex round 1 REJECT (2 P1, 2 P2), round 2 REJECT (admission bypass through a cached module; shared :primed marker between profiles, both in the linked-REPL wiring added in the fix round), a four-family mob (codex gpt-6.1-sol, fable-5.1, glm-5.3, deepseek-v4-pro; qwen via cmd returned only a preamble twice) unanimously ruled option B, opus narrowed the tree (linked REPL path, antlr-linked catalog entry and admission staging removed; py/run-session kept so no re-mint; removed tests parked at collab/1792201000000-parked-linked-repl-tests.cljc.txt for F2), codex round 3 APPROVE-WITH-NITS, \\\"No open in-scope P0/P1\\\". Mob consolidation: collab/1792200000000-mob-consolidation.md.\\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:11214:Done since the 08:30 entry (all on origin/master): 01d004b5 AD-0 (section 7.5 \\\"Admission: the trust question\\\" in yin.vm.linker.dht.md; ruling 19, L-e row and I3 note reworded; dao.shibi.md cross-reference; codex APPROVE); bdaed7ff fix: regenerate dht-import-v1.edn after master's BLAKE3 manifest change and move the artifact's spit into the generator (the stale artifact was my I3 landing miss); 438531ec + 0e549b72 AD-1 (yin.repl.admission seam, admission pair, consuming drain, retirement interval, closed allow answers, `--dht-trust` flag and explicit `:admission` on boot; codex round 1 REJECT P1/P2, round 2 APPROVE-WITH-NITS). The owner asked for a retroactive codex review of the two mechanical master changes (bdaed7ff; the BLAKE3 golden re-mint inside 544e99e1): both APPROVED, no findings. The four-family mob (codex, fable, glm, deepseek) and a late non-independent qwen answer are in collab/1792200000000-mob-consolidation.md; its Q1 ruling B is what landed as I3.\\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:11216:IN FLIGHT at handoff (do not kill; check, they may have finished): (a) opus AD-2 in /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ad2 (branch admission-ad2, UNCOMMITTED): deletes `principal-admiss