e retraction index was not reported\\\"\\ntest/yin/vm/linker/dht_end_to_end_test.cljc:401:        (testing \\\"(yin.link/names): both retractions are global, each once\\\"\\ntest/yin/vm/linker/dht_end_to_end_test.cljc:402:          (is (= #{[:dangling-retraction principal (jing/segment-key\\ntest/yin/vm/linker/dht_end_to_end_test.cljc:404:                   [:dangling-retraction principal r1-id]}\\ntest/yin/vm/linker/dht_end_to_end_test.cljc:410:          (is (not-any? #(= :dangling-retraction (:reason %)) (:diagnostics\\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/ledger_test.cljc:144:  (testing \\\"a retraction: the ledger is add-only\\\"\\ntest/yin/vm/linker/head_follow_test.cljc:80:(defn- retraction\\ntest/yin/vm/linker/head_follow_test.cljc:82:  (let [env {:yin.module/op :retract\\ntest/yin/vm/linker/head_follow_test.cljc:108:  \\\"`history` with one more transaction: alib retracted from `v1` and\\ntest/yin/vm/linker/head_follow_test.cljc:111:  (conj history [(retraction key (assertion key 'alib v1 1) 2)\\ntest/yin/repl/store_test.cljc:1311:;; Rehydration fidelity over a published fixture: several `t`, a retraction,\\ntest/yin/repl/store_test.cljc:1324:   and occurs nowhere but in `m`; and the retraction of the first fact.\\\"\\ntest/yin/repl/store_test.cljc:1372:(deftest a-restart-restores-every-transaction-group-history-row-and-retraction\\ntest/yin/repl/store_test.cljc:1400:              \\\"history rows: every assertion and the retraction, each at its\\ntest/yin/repl/store_test.cljc:1403:              \\\"the current view applies the retraction\\\"))\\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:1767:              \\\"republishing with a new manifest retracts, then asserts\\\"\\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:1782:                (is (= [[:assert 1] [:retract 2] [:assert 3]]\\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:1857:        (is (= [[:assert 1] [:retract 2] [:assert 3]]\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794220000000-architect-wedge-findings-gate.kimi-k3.1-pro.stdout.log:25:{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"tool_T6TmVh30cP4Ksq7XVJir3jUN\",\"content\":\"1\\t(ns d2-wedge-min-repro\\n2\\t  \\\"The minimized reproduction of the H3-1 'wedge' — which is a false\\n3\\t  negative, not a cycle.\\n4\\t\\n5\\t  What round 1 measured as 'the evaluator session terminates': a probe that\\n6\\t  built `semantic/create-vm` + `tu/make-observer-session` and called\\n7\\t  `observer/run-on-stream` — but never appended the fixture to the session\\n8\\t  medium (no `tu/queue-rows!`). An observer session over an empty medium\\n9\\t  loads nothing and runs nothing, and a fresh SemanticVM is `:halted? true`\\n10\\t  before any program (yin.vm.semantic/create-vm mints `:halted? true`), so\\n11\\t  the probe read 'halted, zero budget spent' off a machine that never\\n12\\t  executed an instruction.\\n13\\t\\n14\\t  This file is the A/B/C pair that isolates it, each arm runnable alone:\\n15\\t\\n16\\t    arm A  reproduces round 1's drive exactly — 0 steps, halted=true,\\n17\\t           the false negative in three lines\\n18\\t    arm B  adds the ONE missing line (tu/queue-rows!) and drives the same\\n19\\t           D2-compiled fixture through the same evaluator session: it\\n20\\t           completes under the 2M budget with the correct outcome —\\n21\\t           there is no non-terminating cycle in the evaluator session,\\n22\\t           the observer coordination, or any encoder layer\\n23\\t    arm C  shrinks the budget to 10000 steps and shows run-bounded's\\n24\\t           exhaustion throw PROPAGATES out of observer/run-on-stream\\n25\\t           (carry-session rethrows; it never feeds the loop), carrying\\n26\\t           the advanced machine under :consumer and the partial session\\n27\\t           under :session — the opt-in recovery data, not a retry cycle.\\n28\\t\\n29\\t  The kernel-c semantic path (`run-guest-machine`) has no encoder session\\n30\\t  in it at any commit: it is tu/make-observer-session + tu/queue-rows! +\\n31\\t  observer/run-on-stream, single stage. The two C lanes differ only in\\n32\\t  machine construction and loader.\\\"\\n33\\t  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\\n34\\t            [dao.stream.observer :as observer]\\n35\\t            [yang.clojure :as yang]\\n36\\t            [yang.clojure-test :as compiler-test]\\n37\\t            [yang.latte-oracle-test :as latte]\\n38\\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\\n39\\t            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\\n40\\t            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\\n41\\t            [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as linearize]\\n42\\t            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\\n43\\t\\n44\\t(def ^:private original-step vm/step)\\n45\\t(def steps (atom 0))\\n46\\t\\n47\\t(defn- counted-step\\n48\\t  [machine]\\n49\\t  (swap! steps inc)\\n50\\t  (original-step machine))\\n51\\t\\n52\\t(defn- fixture-ast\\n53\\t  \\\"The D2-compiled check-assume-have-discharge fixture, as kernel-c sees it.\\\"\\n54\\t  []\\n55\\t  (let [fixture (first (filter #(= :check-assume-have-discharge (:id %))\\n56\\t                               (:fixtures (deref #'latte/kernel-gate-corpus))))\\n57\\t        compiled ((deref #'latte/kernel-compile) fixture)]\\n58\\t    (when-not (= :compiled (:status compiled))\\n59\\t      (throw (ex-info \\\"fixture no longer compiles\\\" {:status (:status compiled)})))\\n60\\t    (:ast compiled)))\\n61\\t\\n62\\t(defn- load-rows\\n63\\t  []\\n64\\t  (vm/fresh-code-loader\\n65\\t    (fn [m rows stamp]\\n66\\t      (vm/check-contract! vm/ast-contract stamp)\\n67\\t      (semantic/load-vector m\\n68\\t                            (:vector (linearize/project-rows rows))\\n69\\t                            vm/semantic-contract))\\n70\\t    vm/ast-contract))\\n71\\t\\n72\\t(defn- bounded-run\\n73\\t  \\\"run-guest-machine's runner, verbatim.\\\"\\n74\\t  [step-limit]\\n75\\t  (fn [machine]\\n76\\t    (loop [v machine n 0]\\n77\\t      (cond\\n78\\t        (or (vm/halted? v) (vm/blocked? v)) v\\n79\\t        (= n step-limit) (throw (ex-info \\\"Guest instruction budget exhausted\\\"\\n80\\t                                         {:lane :semantic :steps n :consumer v}))\\n81\\t        :else (recur (vm/step v) (inc n))))))\\n82\\t\\n83\\t(defn- bounded [x]\\n84\\t  (let [s (pr-str x)]\\n85\\t    (if (> (count s) 200) (subs s 0 200) s)))\\n86\\t\\n87\\t(defn- arm-a-round-1-drive\\n88\\t  []\\n89\\t  (reset! steps 0)\\n90\\t  (let [machine (semantic/create-vm {:make-stream tu/make-stream\\n91\\t                                     :capability-secret tu/secret\\n92\\t                                     :modules (deref #'compiler-test/library-modules)})\\n93\\t        session (tu/make-observer-session machine)] ;; medium is EMPTY\\n94\\t    (with-redefs [vm/step counted-step]\\n95\\t      (let [done (observer/run-on-stream session\\n96\\t                                         engine/ready-for-ingress?\\n97\\t                                         (load-rows)\\n98\\t                                         (bounded-run 2000000))]\\n99\\t        {:steps @steps\\n100\\t         :halted (vm/halted? (:consumer done))\\n101\\t         :blocked (vm/blocked? (:consumer done))\\n102\\t         :queue-line :absent}))))\\n103\\t\\n104\\t(defn- arm-b-true-drive\\n105\\t  []\\n106\\t  (reset! steps 0)\\n107\\t  (let [ast (fixture-ast)\\n108\\t        machine (semantic/create-vm {:make-stream tu/make-stream\\n109\\t                                     :capability-secret tu/secret\\n110\\t                                     :modules ((deref #'latte/oracle-registry) yang/kind-module)})\\n111\\t        session (tu/make-observer-session machine)]\\n112\\t    (with-redefs [vm/step counted-step]\\n113\\t      (let [done (as-> session s\\n114\\t                  (tu/queue-rows! s ast) ;; <- the ONE line round 1 omitted\\n115\\t                  (observer/run-on-stream s engine/ready-for-ingress?\\n116\\t                                          (load-rows) (bounded-run 2000000)))\\n117\\t            m (:consumer done)]\\n118\\t        {:steps @steps\\n119\\t         :halted (vm/halted? m)\\n120\\t         :blocked (vm/blocked? m)\\n121\\t         :outcome (bounded (vm/value m))}))))\\n122\\t\\n123\\t(defn- arm-c-exhaustion-propagates\\n124\\t  []\\n125\\t  (reset! steps 0)\\n126\\t  (let [ast (fixture-ast)\\n127\\t        machine (semantic/create-vm {:make-stream tu/make-stream\\n128\\t                                     :capability-secret tu/secret\\n129\\t                                     :modules ((deref #'latte/oracle-registry) yang/kind-module)})\\n130\\t        session (tu/queue-rows! (tu/make-observer-session machine) ast)]\\n131\\t    (try\\n132\\t      (with-redefs [vm/step counted-step]\\n133\\t        (observer/run-on-stream session engine/ready-for-ingress?\\n134\\t                                (load-rows) (bounded-run 10000))\\n135\\t        {:propagated false})\\n136\\t      (catch clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo e\\n137\\t        (let [d (ex-data e)\\n138\\t              consumer (:consumer d)]\\n139\\t          {:propagated true\\n140\\t           :message (ex-message e)\\n141\\t           :data-has-consumer (contains? d :consumer)\\n142\\t           :data-has-session (contains? d :session)\\n143\\t           :consumer-advanced {:halted (:halted? consumer)\\n144\\t                               :blocked (:blocked? consumer)\\n145\\t                               :cont-depth (count (:k consumer))\\n146\\t                               :control (select-keys (:control consumer) [:segment :pc])}\\n147\\t           :cause-preserved (some? (ex-cause e))})))))\\n148\\t\\n149\\t(defn- arm-d-gate-freeze-mechanism\\n150\\t  \\\"What the gate does with the exhaustion throw: kernel-attempt's catch\\n151\\t  expands the exception data with `evidence-data` — dissoc'ing :session but\\n152\\t  NOT :consumer, which after a full 2M-step run is the entire advanced\\n153\\t  machine. This arm reproduces exactly that expansion in isolation, under a\\n154\\t  wall bound with a stack dump, so the gate's post-exhaustion freeze is\\n155\\t  attributable without running the corpus.\\\"\\n156\\t  []\\n157\\t  (let [ast (fixture-ast)\\n158\\t        modules ((deref #'latte/oracle-registry) yang/kind-module)]\\n159\\t    (try\\n160\\t      (compiler-test/run-guest-machine ast modules :walker 2000000)\\n161\\t      {:exhausted false}\\n162\\t      (catch clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo e\\n163\\t        (let [data (dissoc (ex-data e) :session)  ;; kernel-attempt's own dissoc\\n164\\t              evidence (deref #'latte/evidence-data)\\n165\\t              t0 (System/currentTimeMillis)\\n166\\t              result (atom {:finished false})\\n167\\t              worker (doto (Thread. (fn []\\n168\\t                                      (try\\n169\\t                                        (let [v (evidence data)]\\n170\\t                                          (reset! result\\n171\\t                                                  {:finished true\\n172\\t                                                   :wall-ms (- (System/currentTimeMillis) t0)\\n173\\t                                                   :walked-keys (count v)}))\\n174\\t                                        (catch Throwable t\\n175\\t                                          (reset! result\\n176\\t                                                  {:finished true\\n177\\t                                                   :wall-ms (- (System/currentTimeMillis) t0)\\n178\\t                                                   :threw (ex-message t)})))))\\n179\\t                          (.setName \\\"arm-d-evidence-walk\\\")\\n180\\t                          (.setDaemon true))]\\n181\\t          (.start worker)\\n182\\t          (loop [waited 0]\\n183\\t            (Thread/sleep 5000)\\n184\\t            (let [r @result]\\n185\\t              (cond\\n186\\t                (:finished r) r\\n187\\t\\n188\\t                (>= waited 120000)\\n189\\t                (do (println :ARM-D-UNFINISHED-AFTER-MS waited)\\n190\\t                    (doseq [frame (take 25 (.getStackTrace worker))]\\n191\\t                      (println \\\"  \\\" (str frame)))\\n192\\t                    (flush)\\n193\\t                    {:finished false :capped-at-ms waited})\\n194\\t\\n195\\t                :else (recur (+ waited 5000))))))))))\\n196\\t\\n197\\t(defn- cycle-scan\\n198\\t  \\\"Identity-based DFS over the same shapes evidence-data/postwalk traverse\\n199\\t  (maps, vectors, seqs, sets, records). Reports unique node count, the\\n200\\t  deepest sharing, and — decisively — whether any container re-enters a node\\n201\\t  already on the DFS path: that is a true cycle, on which clojure.walk's\\n202\\t  postwalk (no seen-set) never terminates. Sharing off the path is normal\\n203\\t  persistent-structure DAG sharing and terminates.\\\"\\n204\\t  [x]\\n205\\t  (let [seen (java.util.IdentityHashMap.)\\n206\\t        path (java.util.IdentityHashMap.)\\n207\\t        nodes (atom 0)\\n208\\t        shared (atom 0)\\n209\\t        cycle (atom nil)\\n210\\t        container? (fn [v] (or (map? v) (vector? v) (sequential? v) (set? v) (record? v)))\\n211\\t        children (fn [v]\\n212\\t                   (cond\\n213\\t                     (map? v) (concat (keys v) (vals v))\\n214\\t                     (record? v) (vals v)\\n215\\t                     :else (seq v)))]\\n216\\t    (letfn [(go [v depth]\\n217\\t              (when (> depth 200000) (throw (ex-info \\\"scan depth cap\\\" {:depth depth})))\\n218\\t              (when (container? v)\\n219\\t                (when (.containsKey path v)\\n220\\t                  (when-not @cycle (reset! cycle {:type (str (class v)) :at-depth depth}))\\n221\\t                  nil)\\n222\\t                (if (.containsKey seen v)\\n223\\t                  (do (swap! shared inc) nil)\\n224\\t                  (do (.put seen v true)\\n225\\t                      (.put path v true)\\n226\\t                      (swap! nodes inc)\\n227\\t                      (doseq [c (children v)] (go c (inc depth)))\\n228\\t                      (.remove path v)))))]\\n229\\t      (try\\n230\\t        (go x 0)\\n231\\t        (catch Throwable t {:scan-threw (ex-message t)}))\\n232\\t      {:unique-containers @nodes\\n233\\t       :shared-revisits @shared\\n234\\t       :cycle @cycle})))\\n235\\t\\n236\\t(defn- arm-e-cycle-scan\\n237\\t  \\\"Scan the exhausted machine itself (the :consumer from arm D's throw) for\\n238\\t  a cycle with the identity DFS above — the difference between an expensive\\n239\\t  finite expansion and a non-terminating one.\\\"\\n240\\t  []\\n241\\t  (let [ast (fixture-ast)\\n242\\t        modules ((deref #'latte/oracle-registry) yang/kind-module)]\\n243\\t    (try\\n244\\t      (compiler-test/run-guest-machine ast modules :walker 2000000)\\n245\\t      {:exhausted false}\\n246\\t      (catch clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo e\\n247\\t        (cycle-scan (:consumer (ex-data e)))))))\\n248\\t\\n249\\t(defn -main\\n250\\t  [& _args]\\n251\\t  (println :PIN {:commit \\\"8ea857c1+min-repro\\\" :fixture :check-assume-have-discharge})\\n252\\t  (println :ARM-A (arm-a-round-1-drive))\\n253\\t  (println :ARM-B (arm-b-true-drive))\\n254\\t  (println :ARM-C (arm-c-exhaustion-propagates))\\n255\\t  (println :ARM-D (arm-d-gate-freeze-mechanism))\\n256\\t  (println :ARM-E (arm-e-cycle-scan))\\n257\\t  (flush))\\n258\\t\\n259\\t(deftest test-h31-wedge-min-repro\\n260\\t  (testing \\\"diagnostic reproduction only — contributes zero coverage\\\"\\n261\\t    (let [a (arm-a-round-1-drive)\\n262\\t          _ (println :ARM-A a)\\n263\\t          b (arm-b-true-drive)\\n264\\t          _ (println :ARM-B b)\\n265\\t          c (arm-c-exhaustion-propagates)\\n266\\t          _ (println :ARM-C c)\\n267\\t          d (arm-d-gate-freeze-mechanism)\\n268\\t          _ (println :ARM-D d)\\n269\\t          e (arm-e-cycle-scan)\\n270\\t          _ (println :ARM-E e)]\\n271\\t      (is (zero? (:steps a)) \\\"arm A reproduces the round-1 false negative: no step ever ran\\\")\\n272\\t      (is (and (:halted a) (not (:blocked a)))\\n273\\t          \\\"arm A's machine reads halted only because create-vm mints :halted? true\\\")\\n274\\t      (is (and (:halted b) (pos? (:steps b)) (< (:steps b) 2000000))\\n275\\t          \\\"arm B: the same session with the fixture queued completes under the budget\\\")\\n276\\t      (is (and (:propagated c) (:data-has-consumer c) (:data-has-session c))\\n277\\t          \\\"arm C: the budget throw escapes run-on-stream carrying its recovery data\\\")\\n278\\t      (is (map? d) \\\"arm D reports the post-exhaustion evidence walk's cost shape\\\")\\n279\\t      (is (map? e) \\\"arm E reports the exhausted machine's cycle scan\\\")\\n280\\t      (flush))))\"}\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794220000000-architect-wedge-findings-gate.kimi-k3.1-pro.stdout.log:26:{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"tool_CuHwmKAboUjQ5MjypPZH73Bv\",\"content\":\"1\\t(ns d2-wedge-probe2\\n2\\t  \\\"H3-1 wedge diagnostic, round 2: drive the REAL kernel-c semantic path.\\n3\\t\\n4\\t  Round 1's probe (test/d2_wedge_probe.clj) never queued the fixture onto\\n5\\t  the session medium — `tu/make-observer-session` mints an EMPTY medium and\\n6\\t  the probe called no queue variant — so its evaluator-session drive was\\n7\\t  vacuous: a fresh SemanticVM is `:halted? true` (yin.vm.semantic/create-vm)\\n8\\t  before any step, and run-on-stream over an empty medium loads nothing and\\n9\\t  runs nothing. Stage A below reproduces that drive and measures its step\\n10\\t  count to confirm the false negative.\\n11\\t\\n12\\t  Stage B re-measures the exact kernel-c semantic path —\\n13\\t  `yang.clojure-test/run-guest-machine`'s semantic branch\\n14\\t  (tu/make-observer-session + tu/queue-rows! + observer/run-on-stream +\\n15\\t  run-bounded over vm/step) — instrumented at vm/step (count, wall time,\\n16\\t  machine entering each step) and at the run-on-stream boundary (ready\\n17\\t  checks, batches loaded, run entries with per-run step deltas), with a\\n18\\t  watchdog that separates the three failure shapes:\\n19\\t\\n20\\t    - BUDGET-THROWN   run-bounded's 2M exhaustion throw reaches the caller\\n21\\t    - WEDGE-IN-STEP   step count frozen: one vm/step never returns; the\\n22\\t                      worker stack trace plus the entering machine are dumped\\n23\\t    - RATE-COLLAPSE   steps still advance but steps/sec decays toward zero;\\n24\\t                      the per-tick rate table plus a final snapshot are dumped\\\"\\n25\\t  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\\n26\\t            [dao.stream.observer :as observer]\\n27\\t            [yang.clojure :as yang]\\n28\\t            [yang.clojure-test :as compiler-test]\\n29\\t            [yang.latte-oracle-test :as latte]\\n30\\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\\n31\\t            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\\n32\\t            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\\n33\\t            [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as linearize]\\n34\\t            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\\n35\\t\\n36\\t(def ^:private original-step vm/step)\\n37\\t(def ^:private original-run-on-stream observer/run-on-stream)\\n38\\t\\n39\\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- instrumentation\\n40\\t\\n41\\t(def steps (atom 0))\\n42\\t(def in-step-nanos (atom 0))\\n43\\t(def recent-durations (atom []))          ;; last 64 step durations, nanos\\n44\\t(def last-machine (volatile! nil))        ;; machine entering the latest step\\n45\\t(def load-count (atom 0))\\n46\\t(def ready-count (atom 0))\\n47\\t(def run-log (atom []))                   ;; one entry per run-on-stream `run`\\n48\\t(def start-ms (atom nil))\\n49\\t\\n50\\t(defn- reset-instrumentation!\\n51\\t  []\\n52\\t  (reset! steps 0)\\n53\\t  (reset! in-step-nanos 0)\\n54\\t  (reset! recent-durations [])\\n55\\t  (vreset! last-machine nil)\\n56\\t  (reset! load-count 0)\\n57\\t  (reset! ready-count 0)\\n58\\t  (reset! run-log [])\\n59\\t  (reset! start-ms (System/currentTimeMillis)))\\n60\\t\\n61\\t(defn- counted-step\\n62\\t  [machine]\\n63\\t  (let [n (swap! steps inc)]\\n64\\t    (when (= n 1) (println :STEP-STARTED) (flush))\\n65\\t    (vreset! last-machine machine)\\n66\\t    (let [t0 (System/nanoTime)\\n67\\t          v (original-step machine)\\n68\\t          t1 (System/nanoTime)\\n69\\t          d (- t1 t0)]\\n70\\t      (swap! in-step-nanos + d)\\n71\\t      (swap! recent-durations (fn [r] (vec (take-last 64 (conj r d)))))\\n72\\t      v)))\\n73\\t\\n74\\t(defn- instrumented-run-on-stream\\n75\\t  [session ready? load run]\\n76\\t  (let [ready?* (fn [c] (swap! ready-count inc) (ready? c))\\n77\\t        load* (fn [c batch] (swap! load-count inc) (load c batch))\\n78\\t        run* (fn [c]\\n79\\t               (let [before @steps]\\n80\\t                 (try\\n81\\t                   (let [v (run c)]\\n82\\t                     (swap! run-log conj {:entry-steps before\\n83\\t                                          :exit-steps @steps\\n84\\t                                          :threw false})\\n85\\t                     v)\\n86\\t                   (catch Throwable t\\n87\\t                     (swap! run-log conj {:entry-steps before\\n88\\t                                          :exit-steps @steps\\n89\\t                                          :threw (ex-message t)})\\n90\\t                     (throw t)))))]\\n91\\t    (original-run-on-stream session ready?* load* run*)))\\n92\\t\\n93\\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- state capture\\n94\\t\\n95\\t(defn- bounded-str\\n96\\t  [x]\\n97\\t  (let [s (pr-str x)]\\n98\\t    (if (> (count s) 240) (str (subs s 0 240) \\\"…\\\") s)))\\n99\\t\\n100\\t(defn- instruction-at\\n101\\t  \\\"The register instruction the machine's :control points at — op and\\n102\\t  operands, bounded. The instruction vector is static code, so its size is\\n103\\t  the compiler's, not the machine's.\\\"\\n104\\t  [machine]\\n105\\t  (try\\n106\\t    (let [{:keys [segment pc]} (:control machine)\\n107\\t          image (get (:code machine) segment)]\\n108\\t      (if (and image (number? pc) (vector? (:vector image)))\\n109\\t        (bounded-str (try (nth (:vector image) pc)\\n110\\t                          (catch Exception e\\n111\\t                            {:nth-failed (ex-message e)})))\\n112\\t        {:segment segment :pc pc :image (nil? image)}))\\n113\\t    (catch Exception e {:unreadable (ex-message e)})))\\n114\\t\\n115\\t(defn- machine-snapshot\\n116\\t  \\\"Bounded view of one machine: no closures, no environments, no stores.\\\"\\n117\\t  [m]\\n118\\t  (when m\\n119\\t    (let [k (:k m)\\n120\\t          top (when (vector? k) (peek k))]\\n121\\t      {:halted? (:halted? m)\\n122\\t       :blocked? (:blocked? m)\\n123\\t       :cont-depth (if (vector? k) (count k) (when k 1))\\n124\\t       :control (when-let [c (:control m)] (select-keys c [:segment :pc]))\\n125\\t       :control-inst (instruction-at m)\\n126\\t       :top-frame (when (map? top) (select-keys top [:type :segment :pc :rd]))\\n127\\t       :wait-set (count (or (:wait-set m) []))\\n128\\t       :ready-queue (count (or (:ready-queue m) []))\\n129\\t       :window-size (count (:window m))\\n130\\t       :value (bounded-str (:value m))})))\\n131\\t\\n132\\t(defn- duration-stats\\n133\\t  []\\n134\\t  (let [rs @recent-durations]\\n135\\t    (when (seq rs)\\n136\\t      (let [sorted (sort rs)]\\n137\\t        {:n (count sorted)\\n138\\t         :min-ns (first sorted)\\n139\\t         :p50-ns (nth sorted (quot (count sorted) 2))\\n140\\t         :max-ns (last sorted)}))))\\n141\\t\\n142\\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- stage A\\n143\\t\\n144\\t(defn- make-load-rows\\n145\\t  []\\n146\\t  (vm/fresh-code-loader\\n147\\t    (fn [m rows stamp]\\n148\\t      (vm/check-contract! vm/ast-contract stamp)\\n149\\t      (semantic/load-vector m\\n150\\t                            (:vector (linearize/project-rows rows))\\n151\\t                            vm/semantic-contract))\\n152\\t    vm/ast-contract))\\n153\\t\\n154\\t(defn- old-probe-bounded-run\\n155\\t  \\\"Round 1's runner, verbatim semantics.\\\"\\n156\\t  [machine]\\n157\\t  (loop [v machine n 0]\\n158\\t    (cond\\n159\\t      (or (vm/halted? v) (vm/blocked? v)) v\\n160\\t      (= n 2000000)\\n161\\t      (throw (ex-info \\\"Guest instruction budget exhausted\\\"\\n162\\t                      {:lane :semantic :steps n :consumer v}))\\n163\\t      :else (recur (vm/step v) (inc n)))))\\n164\\t\\n165\\t(defn- stage-a-vacuity\\n166\\t  \\\"Reproduce round 1's evaluator-session drive exactly — including its\\n167\\t  missing queue step — and measure how many steps it actually executed.\\\"\\n168\\t  []\\n169\\t  (println :STAGE-A :round-1-probe-reproduction\\n170\\t           {:medium :empty-at-start :queue :absent-as-in-round-1})\\n171\\t  (flush)\\n172\\t  (reset-instrumentation!)\\n173\\t  (let [fixture (first (filter #(= :check-assume-have-discharge (:id %))\\n174\\t                               (:fixtures (deref #'latte/kernel-gate-corpus))))\\n175\\t        ;; round 1 compiled the fixture and never used the result; the call\\n176\\t        ;; itself is kept so stage A matches that run's cost shape\\n177\\t        _ ((deref #'latte/kernel-compile) fixture)\\n178\\t        lm (deref #'compiler-test/library-modules)\\n179\\t        machine (semantic/create-vm {:make-stream tu/make-stream\\n180\\t                                     :capability-secret tu/secret\\n181\\t                                     :modules lm})\\n182\\t        session (tu/make-observer-session machine)]\\n183\\t    (with-redefs [vm/step counted-step\\n184\\t                  observer/run-on-stream instrumented-run-on-stream]\\n185\\t      (let [done (observer/run-on-stream session\\n186\\t                                         engine/ready-for-ingress?\\n187\\t                                         (make-load-rows)\\n188\\t                                         old-probe-bounded-run)]\\n189\\t        (println :STAGE-A-RESULT\\n190\\t                 {:steps @steps\\n191\\t                  :loads @load-count\\n192\\t                  :halted (vm/halted? (:consumer done))\\n193\\t                  :blocked (vm/blocked? (:consumer done))\\n194\\t                  :verdict (if (zero? @steps)\\n195\\t                             :VACUOUS-no-program-ever-loaded\\n196\\t                             :REAL-round1-was-valid)})\\n197\\t        (flush)))))\\n198\\t\\n199\\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- stage B\\n200\\t\\n201\\t(def ^:private tick-ms 10000)\\n202\\t(def ^:private wall-cap-ms 1800000)\\n203\\t(def ^:private frozen-ticks 3)\\n204\\t\\n205\\t(defn- print-tick\\n206\\t  [t steps-prev]\\n207\\t  (let [n @steps\\n208\\t        in-step-ms (quot @in-step-nanos 1000000)\\n209\\t        elapsed (quot (- (System/currentTimeMillis) @start-ms) 1000)\\n210\\t        m @last-machine\\n211\\t        k (:k m)\\n212\\t        stats (duration-stats)\\n213\\t        rate (if (>= steps-prev 0)\\n214\\t               (quot (* (- n steps-prev) 1000) t)\\n215\\t               :first-tick)]\\n216\\t    (println :TICK {:s elapsed :steps n :in-step-ms in-step-ms\\n217\\t                    :steps-per-s-last-tick rate\\n218\\t                    :step-ns stats\\n219\\t                    :cont-depth (when (vector? k) (count k))\\n220\\t                    :loads @load-count :runs (count @run-log)})\\n221\\t    (flush)\\n222\\t    n))\\n223\\t\\n224\\t(defn- dump-state\\n225\\t  [worker label]\\n226\\t  (println label {:steps @steps\\n227\\t                  :in-step-ms (quot @in-step-nanos 1000000)\\n228\\t                  :loads @load-count\\n229\\t                  :ready-checks @ready-count\\n230\\t                  :runs @run-log\\n231\\t                  :entering-machine (machine-snapshot @last-machine)})\\n232\\t  (when worker\\n233\\t    (println :WORKER-STACK)\\n234\\t    (doseq [frame (take 60 (.getStackTrace worker))]\\n235\\t      (println \\\"  \\\" (str frame)))\\n236\\t    (flush)))\\n237\\t\\n238\\t(defn- stage-b-real-path\\n239\\t  []\\n240\\t  (println :STAGE-B :real-kernel-c-semantic-path\\n241\\t           {:driver 'yang.clojure-test/run-guest-machine\\n242\\t            :fixture :check-assume-have-discharge\\n243\\t            :step-limit 2000000\\n244\\t            :wall-cap-ms wall-cap-ms})\\n245\\t  (flush)\\n246\\t  (reset-instrumentation!)\\n247\\t  (let [fixture (first (filter #(= :check-assume-have-discharge (:id %))\\n248\\t                               (:fixtures (deref #'latte/kernel-gate-corpus))))\\n249\\t        compiled ((deref #'latte/kernel-compile) fixture)\\n250\\t        _ (when-not (= :compiled (:status compiled))\\n251\\t            (println :STAGE-B-BLOCKED-AT-COMPILE\\n252\\t                     (select-keys compiled [:status :blocked-by]))\\n253\\t            (flush))\\n254\\t        ast (:ast compiled)\\n255\\t        modules ((deref #'latte/oracle-registry) yang/kind-module)\\n256\\t        result (atom {:kind :none})\\n257\\t        worker (Thread. (fn []\\n258\\t                          (try\\n259\\t                            (let [machine (compiler-test/run-guest-machine\\n260\\t                                            ast modules :semantic 2000000)]\\n261\\t                              (reset! result {:kind :returned\\n262\\t                                              :machine (machine-snapshot machine)\\n263\\t                                              :value (bounded-str (vm/value machine))}))\\n264\\t                            (catch Throwable t\\n265\\t                              (reset! result\\n266\\t                                      {:kind :threw\\n267\\t                                       :class (str (class t))\\n268\\t                                       :message (ex-message t)\\n269\\t                                       :data-keys (vec (keys (ex-data t)))\\n270\\t                                       :consumer (machine-snapshot\\n271\\t                                                   (:consumer (ex-data t)))\\n272\\t                                       :session-consumer (machine-snapshot\\n273\\t                                                           (:consumer\\n274\\t                                                             (:session (ex-data t))))})))))]\\n275\\t    (.setName worker \\\"wedge-worker\\\")\\n276\\t    (.setDaemon worker true)\\n277\\t    (with-redefs [vm/step counted-step\\n278\\t                  observer/run-on-stream instrumented-run-on-stream]\\n279\\t      (.start worker)\\n280\\t      (loop [prev -1 frozen 0]\\n281\\t        (Thread/sleep (long tick-ms))\\n282\\t        (let [alive (.isAlive worker)\\n283\\t              n (when alive (print-tick tick-ms prev))]\\n284\\t          (cond\\n285\\t            (not alive)\\n286\\t            (do (println :WORKER-DONE (assoc @result\\n287\\t                                             :steps @steps\\n288\\t                                             :in-step-ms (quot @in-step-nanos 1000000)\\n289\\t                                             :loads @load-count\\n290\\t                                             :ready-checks @ready-count\\n291\\t                                             :runs @run-log))\\n292\\t                (flush)\\n293\\t                (condp = (:kind @result)\\n294\\t                  :returned (System/exit 0)\\n295\\t                  :threw (System/exit 1)\\n296\\t                  (System/exit 4)))\\n297\\t\\n298\\t            (>= (- (System/currentTimeMillis) @start-ms) (long wall-cap-ms))\\n299\\t            (do (dump-state worker :RATE-COLLAPSE-WALL-CAP) (System/exit 2))\\n300\\t\\n301\\t            (and n (= n prev))\\n302\\t            (do (when (>= (inc frozen) frozen-ticks)\\n303\\t                  (dump-state worker :WEDGE-CONFIRMED-IN-STEP)\\n304\\t                  (System/exit 3))\\n305\\t                (recur (or n prev) (inc frozen)))\\n306\\t\\n307\\t            :else (recur (or n prev) 0)))))))\\n308\\t\\n309\\t(defn -main\\n310\\t  [& _args]\\n311\\t  (println :PIN {:commit \\\"8ea857c1+probe2\\\"\\n312\\t                 :fixture :check-assume-have-discharge\\n313\\t                 :lane :semantic\\n314\\t                 :budget \\\"2M instrumented steps\\\"\\n315\\t                 :jvm (str (System/getProperty \\\"java.version\\\"))})\\n316\\t  (flush)\\n317\\t  (stage-a-vacuity)\\n318\\t  (stage-b-real-path))\\n319\\t\\n320\\t(deftest test-h31-wedge-probe2\\n321\\t  (testing \\\"diagnostic probe only — contributes zero coverage\\\"\\n322\\t    (-main)\\n323\\t    (is true)))\\n324\\t\\n325\\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- stage C\\n326\\t\\n327\\t;; Stage B showed the fixture's own semantic cell completes (1.1M steps,\\n328\\t;; seconds of stepping) when driven alone. The reported stalls were observed\\n329\\t;; on the whole-corpus gate, so stage C drives the gate itself — every\\n330\\t;; fixture's A/B/compile/walker/semantic legs — under timing wrappers and\\n331\\t;; the vm/step counter, with freeze detection that dumps the worker stack\\n332\\t;; wherever the run stops advancing (C lane stepping, host A/B eval, or\\n333\\t;; anywhere else).\\n334\\t\\n335\\t(def ^:private gate-frozen-ticks 30)          ;; 5 min without a step\\n336\\t(def ^:private gate-wall-cap-ms 5400000)      ;; the longest observed trial\\n337\\t\\n338\\t(defn- wall-ms-since\\n339\\t  [t0]\\n340\\t  (- (System/currentTimeMillis) t0))\\n341\\t\\n342\\t(defn- stage-c-gate\\n343\\t  []\\n344\\t  (println :STAGE-C :full-differential-gate\\n345\\t           {:test 'yang.latte-oracle-test/test-kernel-differential-gate\\n346\\t            :freeze-ticks gate-frozen-ticks\\n347\\t            :wall-cap-ms gate-wall-cap-ms})\\n348\\t  (flush)\\n349\\t  (reset-instrumentation!)\\n350\\t  (let [gate-t0 (System/currentTimeMillis)\\n351\\t        leg (fn [label f]\\n352\\t              (fn [& args]\\n353\\t                (let [t0 (System/currentTimeMillis)\\n354\\t                      before @steps\\n355\\t                      r (apply f args)]\\n356\\t                  (println :LEG label\\n357\\t                           {:wall-ms (- (System/currentTimeMillis) t0)\\n358\\t                            :steps (- @steps before)\\n359\\t                            :arg0 (bounded-str (first args))})\\n360\\t                  (flush)\\n361\\t                  r)))\\n362\\t        orig-kernel-a (deref #'latte/kernel-a)\\n363\\t        orig-kernel-b (deref #'latte/kernel-b)\\n364\\t        orig-kernel-compile (deref #'latte/kernel-compile)\\n365\\t        orig-kernel-c (deref #'latte/kernel-c)\\n366\\t        orig-kernel-row (deref #'latte/kernel-row)\\n367\\t        kernel-c* (fn [compiled lane]\\n368\\t                    (let [before @steps]\\n369\\t                      (println :C-ENTER {:lane lane\\n370\\t                                         :at-steps before\\n371\\t                                         :total-s (quot (wall-ms-since gate-t0) 1000)})\\n372\\t                      (flush)\\n373\\t                      (let [t0 (System/currentTimeMillis)\\n374\\t                            r (orig-kernel-c compiled lane)]\\n375\\t                        (println :C-EXIT {:lane lane\\n376\\t                                          :wall-ms (- (System/currentTimeMillis) t0)\\n377\\t                                          :steps (- @steps before)\\n378\\t                                          :status (:status r)\\n379\\t                                          :outcome-tag (-> r :outcome first)})\\n380\\t                        (flush)\\n381\\t                        r)))\\n382\\t        result (atom {:kind :none})\\n383\\t        worker (Thread. (fn []\\n384\\t                          (try\\n385\\t                            ;; test-var output goes to this process's stdout\\n386\\t                            ;; on purpose: the gate's own KERNEL-FIXTURE lines\\n387\\t                            ;; are the live mid-fixture progress signal.\\n388\\t                            (clojure.test/test-var\\n389\\t                              #'yang.latte-oracle-test/test-kernel-differential-gate)\\n390\\t                            (reset! result {:kind :returned\\n391\\t                                            :wall-ms (wall-ms-since gate-t0)})\\n392\\t                            (catch Throwable t\\n393\\t                              (reset! result {:kind :threw\\n394\\t                                              :class (str (class t))\\n395\\t                                              :message (ex-message t)\\n396\\t                                              :wall-ms (wall-ms-since gate-t0)})))))]\\n397\\t    (.setName worker \\\"wedge-worker\\\")\\n398\\t    (.setDaemon worker true)\\n399\\t    (with-redefs-fn {#'vm/step counted-step\\n400\\t                     #'observer/run-on-stream instrumented-run-on-stream\\n401\\t                     #'latte/kernel-a (leg :a orig-kernel-a)\\n402\\t                     #'latte/kernel-b (leg :b orig-kernel-b)\\n403\\t                     #'latte/kernel-compile (leg :compile orig-kernel-compile)\\n404\\t                     #'latte/kernel-c kernel-c*\\n405\\t                     #'latte/kernel-row (leg :row orig-kernel-row)}\\n406\\t      (fn []\\n407\\t        (.start worker)\\n408\\t        (loop [prev -1 frozen 0]\\n409\\t          (Thread/sleep (long tick-ms))\\n410\\t          (let [alive (.isAlive worker)\\n411\\t                n (when alive (print-tick tick-ms prev))]\\n412\\t            (cond\\n413\\t              (not alive)\\n414\\t              (do (println :GATE-DONE (assoc @result\\n415\\t                                             :steps @steps\\n416\\t                                             :in-step-ms (quot @in-step-nanos 1000000)\\n417\\t                                             :wall-ms (wall-ms-since gate-t0)\\n418\\t                                             :runs @run-log))\\n419\\t                  (flush)\\n420\\t                  (condp = (:kind @result)\\n421\\t                    :returned (System/exit 0)\\n422\\t                    :threw (System/exit 1)\\n423\\t                    (System/exit 4)))\\n424\\t\\n425\\t              (>= (- (System/currentTimeMillis) gate-t0) (long gate-wall-cap-ms))\\n426\\t              (do (dump-state worker :GATE-WALL-CAP-REACHED) (System/exit 2))\\n427\\t\\n428\\t              (and n (= n prev))\\n429\\t              (do (when (>= (inc frozen) gate-frozen-ticks)\\n430\\t                    (dump-state worker :GATE-FROZEN-5MIN)\\n431\\t                    (System/exit 3))\\n432\\t                  (recur (or n prev) (inc frozen)))\\n433\\t\\n434\\t              :else (recur (or n prev) 0))))))))\\n435\\t\\n436\\t(deftest test-h31-wedge-probe2-gate\\n437\\t  (testing \\\"diagnostic probe only — contributes zero coverage\\\"\\n438\\t    (stage-c-gate)\\n439\\t    (is true)))\\n440\\t\\n441\\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- stage D\\n442\\t\\n443\\t;; The in-gate freeze sat in check-assume-have-discharge's WALKER cell: it\\n444\\t;; consumed exactly its whole 2,000,000-step budget and then the run never\\n445\\t;; returned while no step advanced. Stage D drives that one cell in\\n446\\t;; isolation — same driver, same instrumentation — to (a) confirm the\\n447\\t;; exhaustion reproduces without the corpus context and (b) capture the\\n448\\t;; bounded exhaustion state: the advanced :consumer's halted/blocked flags,\\n449\\t;; continuation depth, control, and the top frame.\\n450\\t\\n451\\t(defn- stage-d-walker\\n452\\t  []\\n453\\t  (println :STAGE-D :walker-cell-in-isolation\\n454\\t           {:driver 'yang.clojure-test/run-guest-machine\\n455\\t            :fixture :check-assume-have-discharge\\n456\\t            :step-limit 2000000})\\n457\\t  (flush)\\n458\\t  (reset-instrumentation!)\\n459\\t  (let [fixture (first (filter #(= :check-assume-have-discharge (:id %))\\n460\\t                               (:fixtures (deref #'latte/kernel-gate-corpus))))\\n461\\t        compiled ((deref #'latte/kernel-compile) fixture)\\n462\\t        ast (:ast compiled)\\n463\\t        modules ((deref #'latte/oracle-registry) yang/kind-module)\\n464\\t        result (atom {:kind :none})\\n465\\t        worker (Thread. (fn []\\n466\\t                          (try\\n467\\t                            (let [machine (compiler-test/run-guest-machine\\n468\\t                                            ast modules :walker 2000000)]\\n469\\t                              (reset! result {:kind :returned\\n470\\t                                              :machine (machine-snapshot machine)}))\\n471\\t                            (catch Throwable t\\n472\\t                              (reset! result\\n473\\t                                      {:kind :threw\\n474\\t                                       :class (str (class t))\\n475\\t                                       :message (ex-message t)\\n476\\t                                       :data-keys (vec (keys (ex-data t)))\\n477\\t                                       :consumer (machine-snapshot\\n478\\t                                                   (:consumer (ex-data t)))\\n479\\t                                       :session-consumer (machine-snapshot\\n480\\t                                                           (:consumer\\n481\\t                                                             (:session (ex-data t))))})))))]\\n482\\t    (.setName worker \\\"wedge-worker\\\")\\n483\\t    (.setDaemon worker true)\\n484\\t    (with-redefs [vm/step counted-step\\n485\\t                  observer/run-on-stream instrumented-run-on-stream]\\n486\\t      (.start worker)\\n487\\t      (loop [prev -1 frozen 0]\\n488\\t        (Thread/sleep (long tick-ms))\\n489\\t        (let [alive (.isAlive worker)\\n490\\t              n (when alive (print-tick tick-ms prev))]\\n491\\t          (cond\\n492\\t            (not alive)\\n493\\t            (do (println :WORKER-DONE (assoc @result\\n494\\t                                             :steps @steps\\n495\\t                                             :in-step-ms (quot @in-step-nanos 1000000)\\n496\\t                                             :loads @load-count\\n497\\t                                             :runs @run-log))\\n498\\t                (flush)\\n499\\t                (condp = (:kind @result)\\n500\\t                  :returned (System/exit 0)\\n501\\t                  :threw (System/exit 1)\\n502\\t                  (System/exit 4)))\\n503\\t\\n504\\t            (>= (- (System/currentTimeMillis) @start-ms) (long wall-cap-ms))\\n505\\t            (do (dump-state worker :RATE-COLLAPSE-WALL-CAP) (System/exit 2))\\n506\\t\\n507\\t            (and n (= n prev))\\n508\\t            (do (when (>= (inc frozen) frozen-ticks)\\n509\\t                  (dump-state worker :WEDGE-CONFIRMED-IN-STEP)\\n510\\t                  (System/exit 3))\\n511\\t                (recur (or n prev) (inc frozen)))\\n512\\t\\n513\\t            :else (recur (or n prev) 0)))))))\\n514\\t\\n515\\t(deftest test-h31-wedge-probe2-walker\\n516\\t  (testing \\\"diagnostic probe only — contributes zero coverage\\\"\\n517\\t    (stage-d-walker)\\n518\\t    (is true)))\\n519\\t\\n520\\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- stage F\\n521\\t\\n522\\t;; The walker cell now exhausts 2M (stage D) while the semantic cell\\n523\\t;; completes at 1.1M (stage B). How far over the budget is the walker?\\n524\\t;; One bounded diagnostic trial at 8M — the H3-1 round's authorized trial\\n525\\t;; ladder — reporting the walker's true completion count, or a second\\n526\\t;; exhaustion. Diagnostic configuration only: NOT an acceptance-budget\\n527\\t;; proposal.\\n528\\t\\n529\\t(defn- stage-f-walker-8m\\n530\\t  []\\n531\\t  (println :STAGE-F :walker-cell-8m-trial\\n532\\t           {:driver 'yang.clojure-test/run-guest-machine\\n533\\t            :fixture :check-assume-have-discharge\\n534\\t            :step-limit 8000000})\\n535\\t  (flush)\\n536\\t  (reset-instrumentation!)\\n537\\t  (let [fixture (first (filter #(= :check-assume-have-discharge (:id %))\\n538\\t                               (:fixtures (deref #'latte/kernel-gate-corpus))))\\n539\\t        compiled ((deref #'latte/kernel-compile) fixture)\\n540\\t        ast (:ast compiled)\\n541\\t        modules ((deref #'latte/oracle-registry) yang/kind-module)\\n542\\t        result (atom {:kind :none})\\n543\\t        worker (Thread. (fn []\\n544\\t                          (try\\n545\\t                            (let [machine (compiler-test/run-guest-machine\\n546\\t                                            ast modules :walker 8000000)]\\n547\\t                              (reset! result {:kind :returned\\n548\\t                                              :steps @steps\\n549\\t                                              :machine (machine-snapshot machine)\\n550\\t                                              :value (bounded-str (vm/value machine))}))\\n551\\t                            (catch Throwable t\\n552\\t                              (reset! result\\n553\\t                                      {:kind :threw\\n554\\t                                       :class (str (class t))\\n555\\t                                       :message (ex-message t)\\n556\\t                                       :steps @steps})))))]\\n557\\t    (.setName worker \\\"wedge-worker\\\")\\n558\\t    (.setDaemon worker true)\\n559\\t    (with-redefs [vm/step counted-step\\n560\\t                  observer/run-on-stream instrumented-run-on-stream]\\n561\\t      (.start worker)\\n562\\t      (loop [prev -1 frozen 0]\\n563\\t        (Thread/sleep (long tick-ms))\\n564\\t        (let [alive (.isAlive worker)\\n565\\t              n (when alive (print-tick tick-ms prev))]\\n566\\t          (cond\\n567\\t            (not alive)\\n568\\t            (do (println :WORKER-DONE (assoc @result\\n569\\t                                             :in-step-ms (quot @in-step-nanos 1000000)\\n570\\t                                             :loads @load-count\\n571\\t                                             :runs @run-log))\\n572\\t                (flush)\\n573\\t                (condp = (:kind @result)\\n574\\t                  :returned (System/exit 0)\\n575\\t                  :threw (System/exit 1)\\n576\\t                  (System/exit 4)))\\n577\\t\\n578\\t            (>= (- (System/currentTimeMillis) @start-ms) (long wall-cap-ms))\\n579\\t            (do (dump-state worker :RATE-COLLAPSE-WALL-CAP) (System/exit 2))\\n580\\t\\n581\\t            (and n (= n prev))\\n582\\t            (do (when (>= (inc frozen) frozen-ticks)\\n583\\t                  (dump-state worker :WEDGE-CONFIRMED-IN-STEP)\\n584\\t                  (System/exit 3))\\n585\\t                (recur (or n prev) (inc frozen)))\\n586\\t\\n587\\t            :else (recur (or n prev) 0)))))))\\n588\\t\\n589\\t(deftest test-h31-wedge-probe2-walker-8m\\n590\\t  (testing \\\"diagnostic probe only — contributes zero coverage\\\"\\n591\\t    (stage-f-walker-8m)\\n592\\t    (is true)))\"}\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794220000000-architect-wedge-findings-gate.kimi-k3.1-pro.stdout.log:27:{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"tool_cjbnlf9Hm5RDggcFuke6YRJF\",\"content\":\"1\\t# H3-1 wedge diagnostic, round 2 — the findings report\\n2\\t\\n3\\tCreated: 2026-11-04 (GMT) · Agent: glm (glm-5.3) · Branch: `hardening3-h3-1` at `8ea857c1`\\n4\\tTask: BRIEF-wedge.md (per the architect's continuation ruling, steps 3–4)\\n5\\tArtifacts: `test/d2_wedge_probe2.clj` (stages A–D, F + gate stage C),\\n6\\t`test/d2_wedge_min_repro.clj` (arms A–E); evidence logs in this directory\\n7\\t(`1794100000000-engineer-h3-1-wedge.probe2-run1|-gate1|-walker1|-walker8m|.minrepro.log`)\\n8\\t\\n9\\t## Verdict in one paragraph\\n10\\t\\n11\\tThere is **no non-terminating loop in the encoder session layer, the observer\\n12\\tcoordination, or the semantic evaluator** — and the kernel-c semantic path\\n13\\tcontains no encoder session at any commit. The round-1 \\\"evaluator terminates /\\n14\\twedge lives in the encoder session layer\\\" split was an artifact of a vacuous\\n15\\tprobe. The gate stall that motivated this round is real, it reproduces, and it\\n16\\tlives **after** the walker cell's legitimate budget exhaustion: the gate's\\n17\\t`kernel-attempt` hands the exhaustion exception's `:consumer` — the entire\\n18\\tadvanced machine — to `evidence-data` → `upstream-record-data`, whose\\n19\\t`clojure.walk/postwalk` re-expands it with five `requiring-resolve` calls per\\n20\\tnode and no cycle guard. That host-side walk, not any VM loop, is what burns\\n21\\t2400s+ with zero guest steps. D2's real regression is smaller and factual: it\\n22\\tpushed this fixture's **walker** cell over the 2M budget (the semantic cell\\n23\\tstill completes at 1.1M).\\n24\\t\\n25\\t## 1. Round 1's probe was vacuous — the layer-location built on it is retracted\\n26\\t\\n27\\t`test/d2_wedge_probe.clj` builds `semantic/create-vm` + `tu/make-observer-session`\\n28\\tand calls `observer/run-on-stream` — but **never queues the fixture onto the\\n29\\tmedium** (no `tu/queue-rows!` anywhere in the file). An observer session over\\n30\\tan empty medium observes nothing (`:retry`/`:ended`), never calls `load`, never\\n31\\tenters `run`. And a fresh `SemanticVM` is minted `:halted? true`\\n32\\t(`src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:432`), so the untouched machine reads \\\"halted\\\".\\n33\\t\\n34\\tMeasured (stage A, `…-probe2-run1.log` in this directory):\\n35\\t\\n36\\t```\\n37\\t:STAGE-A-RESULT {:steps 0, :loads 0, :halted true, :blocked false,\\n38\\t                 :verdict :VACUOUS-no-program-ever-loaded}\\n39\\t```\\n40\\t\\n41\\tZero steps. The \\\"terminates, halted, well under 2M\\\" measurement in commit\\n42\\t`8ea857c1` measured a machine that never executed an instruction.\\n43\\t\\n44\\tThe same commit message's premise — \\\"kernel-c wraps the machine in\\n45\\ttu/make-encoder-session + encoder/forward-on-stream\\\" — is false at `8ea857c1`\\n46\\tand at every commit since `run-guest-machine` was introduced (`7723c6ae`): the\\n47\\tkernel-c path is `tu/make-observer-session` + `tu/queue-rows!`/`queue-ast!` +\\n48\\tone `observer/run-on-stream` call (`test/yang/clojure_test.clj:1995-2009`),\\n49\\tsingle stage, no encoder. The only encoder references in `clojure_test.clj`\\n50\\tare the descriptor tests (lines 785, 1028, 1047).\\n51\\t\\n52\\t## 2. The real kernel-c semantic cell completes (stage B)\\n53\\t\\n54\\tDriving the exact kernel-c semantic call —\\n55\\t`run-guest-machine ast (oracle-registry yang/kind-module) :semantic 2000000` —\\n56\\tinstrumented at `vm/step` and at the `run-on-stream` boundary:\\n57\\t\\n58\\t```\\n59\\t:WORKER-DONE {:kind :returned,\\n60\\t              :steps 1105792, :in-step-ms 2535, :loads 1, :ready-checks 3,\\n61\\t              :runs [{:entry-steps 0, :exit-steps 1105792, :threw false}],\\n62\\t              :halted true, :blocked false,\\n63\\t              :value [:yin.k/ok [:ok [(<a>) (Π [A ✳] (Π [B ✳] …))]]]}\\n64\\t```\\n65\\t\\n66\\t1,105,792 steps (55% of budget), 2.5 s of stepping, correct proof outcome. This\\n67\\tmatches the pre-D2 measurement (`0dc54289`: both fixtures complete inside 2M\\n68\\tafter the call-lowering fix) — D2 did not make the semantic cell explode.\\n69\\t\\n70\\t## 3. The observer/encoder layer cannot be the loop (code + measurement)\\n71\\t\\n72\\tThe brief's candidate — the budget throw caught by `carry-session` and fed back\\n73\\tvia `consumer-left-by-run` — does not exist:\\n74\\t\\n75\\t- `carry-session` (`src/cljc/dao/stream/observer.cljc:211-214`) **rethrows**:\\n76\\t  `(throw (ex-info … (assoc (ex-data e) :session session) e))`. Both catch\\n77\\t  sites in `run-on-stream` (`observer.cljc:250-255` and `277-282`) call it\\n78\\t  directly; neither recurs.\\n79\\t- `consumer-left-by-run` (`observer.cljc:183-196`) only reads `:consumer` from\\n80\\t  the exception's data to attach to the carried `:session`. It is never a loop\\n81\\t  variable; no caller re-enters `run` with it inside this harness.\\n82\\t- `run-on-stream`'s loop re-enters only on `:advance` (a batch observed), `:gap`\\n83\\t  (recovery cursor), or not-ready→run→ready. This harness queues exactly one\\n84\\t  batch: measured `loads 1, runs 1`.\\n85\\t- Arm C of the minimized reproduction drives the semantic cell at a 10,000-step\\n86\\t  budget: the exhaustion throw **propagates out** of `run-on-stream` with\\n87\\t  `:consumer` (advanced machine), `:session` (partial session), and the cause\\n88\\t  preserved. Recovery is opt-in data for callers; there is no retry cycle.\\n89\\t\\n90\\t## 4. Where the gate actually stalls — the exact site, caught in the act\\n91\\t\\n92\\tStage C drove the full 106-fixture differential gate\\n93\\t(`test-kernel-differential-gate`) under the same instrumentation with a\\n94\\tfreeze detector. It froze mid-corpus, in `check-assume-have-discharge`\\n95\\t(fixture 50 of 106), **inside the walker C cell** — the opposite lane from the\\n96\\tD2 report's attribution:\\n97\\t\\n98\\t```\\n99\\t:LEG :a …wall-ms 5      (check-assume-have-discharge)\\n100\\t:LEG :b …wall-ms 89\\n101\\t:LEG :compile …wall-ms 51\\n102\\t:C-ENTER {:lane :walker, :at-steps 3786531, :total-s 91}\\n103\\t   … steps advance to 5786531 (= 3786531 + exactly 2000000) in ~20 s …\\n104\\t   … then zero steps for ≥300 s; no :C-EXIT ever prints; detector fired\\n105\\t```\\n106\\t\\n107\\tThe captured worker stack (top frames, full dump in\\n108\\t`1794100000000-engineer-h3-1-wedge.probe2-gate1.log` in this directory):\\n109\\t\\n110\\t```\\n111\\tclojure.lang.Var.getThreadBinding → requiring-resolve\\n112\\tyang.latte_oracle_test$upstream_fn.invokeStatic        (latte_oracle_test.clj:286)\\n113\\tyang.latte_oracle_test$upstream_record_data$…invoke    (latte_oracle_test.clj:1025)\\n114\\tclojure.walk$postwalk → into → reduce → LazySeq.force → clojure.walk$postwalk …\\n115\\t```\\n116\\t\\n117\\tThe causal chain, with line references:\\n118\\t\\n119\\t1. `run-bounded` (`test/yang/clojure_test.clj:1987-1993`) counts 2,000,000\\n120\\t   walker steps — the walker cell of this fixture now **exhausts** the budget\\n121\\t   (it completed inside 2M before D2) — and throws\\n122\\t   `\\\"Guest instruction budget exhausted\\\"` with `{:lane … :steps … :consumer v}`\\n123\\t   (`clojure_test.clj:1991-1992`; the `:consumer` addition is the H3-1 fix\\n124\\t   round's own one-line harness change).\\n125\\t2. `run-on-stream`'s run-catch (`observer.cljc:277-282`) wraps via\\n126\\t   `carry-session` — a cheap rethrow adding `:session`.\\n127\\t3. `kernel-c`'s body runs inside `kernel-attempt`\\n128\\t   (`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:1659-1671`), whose catch builds\\n129\\t   `:data (evidence-data (dissoc (ex-data e) :session))` — it strips `:session`\\n130\\t   but **not `:consumer`**, so the entire advanced machine enters\\n131\\t   `evidence-data`.\\n132\\t4. `evidence-data` (`latte_oracle_test.clj:1645-1656`) hits `(record? x)` — the\\n133\\t   machine is a record — and calls `upstream-record-data`\\n134\\t   (`latte_oracle_test.clj:1014-1028`): a `clojure.walk/postwalk` over the\\n135\\t   whole machine that calls `(upstream-fn pred)` — i.e.\\n136\\t   `requiring-resolve` (`latte_oracle_test.clj:284-286`) — **five times per\\n137\\t   node**, then `evidence-data` recurses into every child, and every child\\n138\\t   record (each VM `Closure`/`Continuation` is a record) triggers another full\\n139\\t   `postwalk` of its subtree.\\n140\\t\\n141\\tThat is the \\\"wedge\\\": an unbounded, zero-guest-step, host-side expansion of the\\n142\\texhausted machine. Whether it is truly non-terminating (a cyclic closure\\n143\\tenvironment — recursive guest functions whose captured env binds their own\\n144\\tclosure record, on which `postwalk`, which has no seen-set, never terminates)\\n145\\tor merely hours-scale (per-record re-walk of shared env chains × five\\n146\\t`requiring-resolve` per node) is settled by the cycle scan in §6.\\n147\\t\\n148\\tThis also re-explains the D2-era observations without the encoder theory: the\\n149\\t2400 s/5400 s \\\"semantic cell wall-clock explosion\\\" runs were this same\\n150\\tpost-exhaustion expansion, mid-corpus, with no per-cell attribution recorded\\n151\\t(\\\"guest-step counts NOT yet captured\\\" in `805d81d6`'s message).\\n152\\t\\n153\\t## 5. The exhausted walker cell in isolation (stage D) — bounded state capture\\n154\\t\\n155\\tSame driver, walker lane, alone (no corpus context):\\n156\\t\\n157\\t```\\n158\\t:WORKER-DONE {:kind :threw, :message \\\"Guest instruction budget exhausted\\\",\\n159\\t              :steps 2000000, :in-step-ms 10591, :loads 1,\\n160\\t              :runs [{:entry-steps 0, :exit-steps 2000000,\\n161\\t                      :threw \\\"Guest instruction budget exhausted\\\"}],\\n162\\t              :data-keys [:lane :steps :consumer :session],\\n163\\t              :consumer {:halted? false, :blocked? false, :cont-depth 1,\\n164\\t                         :control {}, :wait-set 0, :ready-queue 0,\\n165\\t                         :value [\\\"_\\\" 6]}}\\n166\\t```\\n167\\t\\n168\\tThe exhaustion itself is fast (≈11 s) and well-behaved: the throw propagates,\\n169\\t`:consumer`/`:session` ride along exactly as the recovery design intends. The\\n170\\tbrief's requested capture at wedge time: the advanced consumer is **neither\\n171\\thalted nor blocked**, continuation depth 1, mid-walk control, gensym value\\n172\\t`[\\\"_\\\" 6]` — the walker died inside fresh-supply generation under the proof\\n173\\tloop, not in any stream or admission machinery.\\n174\\t\\n175\\t## 6. Minimized reproduction — `test/d2_wedge_min_repro.clj`\\n176\\t\\n177\\tFive arms, each runnable alone (`clojure -M:test -n d2-wedge-min-repro -v\\n178\\td2-wedge-min-repro/test-h31-wedge-min-repro`, ≈4–6 min):\\n179\\t\\n180\\t- **arm A** — round 1's drive, verbatim (session, no queue):\\n181\\t  `{0 steps, halted true}` — the false negative in three lines.\\n182\\t- **arm B** — the same session plus the one omitted line (`tu/queue-rows!`):\\n183\\t  completes at **1,105,792 steps**, halted, correct outcome.\\n184\\t- **arm C** — semantic at a 10,000-step budget: the throw escapes\\n185\\t  `run-on-stream` carrying `:consumer` + `:session`; recovery is opt-in.\\n186\\t- **arm D** — the gate freeze mechanism, isolated: drive the walker cell to its\\n187\\t  exhaustion throw, then time exactly kernel-attempt's\\n188\\t  `(evidence-data (dissoc ex-data :session))` under a 120 s cap with a stack\\n189\\t  dump. Result: **unfinished after the 120 s cap** — stack shows the same\\n190\\t  `clojure.walk$postwalk` recursion the gate freeze showed. The walker drive\\n191\\t  itself took ≈11 s; the post-throw expansion is >10× that and still running\\n192\\t  when capped.\\n193\\t- **arm E** — an identity-based DFS cycle scan over the exhausted `:consumer`\\n194\\t  (the same shapes `evidence-data`/`postwalk` traverse), reporting unique\\n195\\t  container count, off-path sharing, and whether any node re-enters the DFS\\n196\\t  path (a true cycle ⇒ `postwalk` never terminates). Result:\\n197\\t  `{:unique-containers 78913, :shared-revisits 3442, :cycle nil}` — **no\\n198\\t  cycle**. The machine is a finite DAG, so the walk terminates *eventually*;\\n199\\t  its cost is the re-expansion: every record child (each VM Closure/\\n200\\t  Continuation) triggers `upstream-record-data`'s own full postwalk of its\\n201\\t  subtree, and the 3,442 sharing points make those subtrees overlap —\\n202\\t  finite-but-astronomical, which is exactly the shape \\\"2400 s × 2 stalled,\\n203\\t  5400 s never returned\\\" describes: not an infinite loop, an expansion that\\n204\\t  had not finished inside the trial window.\\n205\\t\\n206\\t## 7. How far over the budget is the walker? (stage F — bounded trial)\\n207\\t\\n208\\tAt an 8,000,000-step budget the walker cell **completes at 2,024,912 steps**\\n209\\t(11.8 s in-step) with the same correct outcome as the semantic cell:\\n210\\t\\n211\\t```\\n212\\t:WORKER-DONE {:kind :returned, :steps 2024912, :halted true,\\n213\\t              :value [:yin.k/ok [:ok [(<a>) (Π [A ✳] …)]]]}\\n214\\t```\\n215\\t\\n216\\tThe walker misses the 2M budget by **24,912 steps — 1.2%**. D2's per-call\\n217\\tpacket dispatch pushed a cell that previously completed inside 2M (commit\\n218\\t`0dc54289`) just barely over, and the harness's post-exhaustion expansion\\n219\\tturned that near-miss into the multi-hour \\\"wedge\\\". The semantic cell needs\\n220\\t1,105,792 (55% of budget).\\n221\\t\\n222\\t## 8. Recommendation\\n223\\t\\n224\\t1. **No yin.vm / observer / encoder architectural ruling is needed.** Nothing\\n225\\t   in `src/cljc/**` non-terminates or misbehaves; the observer recovery\\n226\\t   protocol did exactly what it is designed to do. No shared-runtime change is\\n227\\t   requested.\\n228\\t2. **The gate stall is a one-line harness defect** in\\n229\\t   `test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:1667`: `kernel-attempt`'s catch feeds the\\n230\\t   exhaustion's `:consumer` machine to `evidence-data`. The comment above that\\n231\\t   very line already classifies `:session` as \\\"diagnostic machinery, not a\\n232\\t   portable domain payload; recursively expanding its closure environments\\n233\\t   duplicates the whole program\\\" — `:consumer` is the same class of payload.\\n234\\t   Proposed next-round fix: `(dissoc (ex-data e) :session :consumer)`, or\\n235\\t   replace `:consumer` with a bounded snapshot (halted/blocked/cont-depth/\\n236\\t   control) before expansion. latte_oracle_test.clj is out of bounds THIS\\n237\\t   round by the brief, so this is a recommendation, not a change.\\n238\\t3. **The D2 landing decision should be re-based on these numbers:** semantic\\n239\\t   cell 1,105,792 steps (completes); walker cell >2,000,000 (exhausts; see §7\\n240\\t   for the true count). The \\\"wall-clock explosion\\\" was the harness amplifying\\n241\\t   the walker's exhaustion, but the exhaustion itself is D2's per-call packet\\n242\\t   dispatch cost on the walker lane. Whatever the landing round decides\\n243\\t   (budget raise is DEFERRED by ruling; trimming the dispatch is a compiler\\n244\\t   change requiring its own scope), it no longer needs to explain a semantic\\n245\\t   wedge.\\n246\\t4. **Correct the record:** commit `8ea857c1`'s conclusion line (\\\"the wedge\\n247\\t   lives in the encoder session layer\\\") should be superseded by this report;\\n248\\t   `test/d2_wedge_probe.clj` should either gain its missing queue line or be\\n249\\t   retired in favor of `d2_wedge_probe2.clj` (this round leaves it untouched —\\n250\\t   it is the previous round's committed artifact and the kimi gate reviews\\n251\\t   before landing).\\n252\\t\\n253\\t## Reproduction ladder (all at `8ea857c1`, JVM 17, -Xss64m, this worktree)\\n254\\t\\n255\\t| run | command | outcome |\\n256\\t|-----|---------|---------|\\n257\\t| stage A+B | `clojure -M:test -n d2-wedge-probe2 -v d2-wedge-probe2/test-h31-wedge-probe2` | A vacuous (0 steps); B returns at 1,105,792 steps |\\n258\\t| stage C (gate) | `clojure -M:test -n d2-wedge-probe2 -v d2-wedge-probe2/test-h31-wedge-probe2-gate` | frozen mid-corpus in the walker cell of check-assume-have-discharge; stack = evidence-data/postwalk; exit 3 by design |\\n259\\t| stage D (walker isolated) | `… -v d2-wedge-probe2/test-h31-wedge-probe2-walker` | throws at exactly 2,000,000 steps in ≈11 s |\\n260\\t| stage F (8M trial) | `… -v d2-wedge-probe2/test-h31-wedge-probe2-walker-8m` | returns at 2,024,912 steps (1.2% over the 2M budget) |\\n261\\t| min-repro A–E | `clojur